    "https://manmetjobs.mmu.ac.uk/jobs/vacancy/ri-project-officer-best-engage-9524-manchester-birley-campus/9421/description/": {
      "title": "R&I Project Officer (BeST Engage)",
      "description": "R&I Project Officer (BeST Engage) - (9524) | Manchester Metropolitan University Careers CareerZone - R&I Project Officer (BeST Engage) (9524) Open toolbar Accessibility Grayscale High contrast Negative contrast Light background Links underline Readable font Reset Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login R&I Project Officer (BeST Engage) - (9524) Are you an organised and proactive project professional looking to support impactful health research? Do you enjoy working with a range of stakeholders to coordinate complex projects, monitor progress and ensure successful delivery? Can you provide high-quality project support to enable researchers to focus on delivering world-leading research? An exciting opportunity has arisen to join the Research & Innovation Team within the Faculty of Health and Education to support the delivery of the NIHR Public Health-funded BeST Engage project. This role is available on a fixed-term basis until 30 June 2028 and is funded through the project. This is an exciting time to join Manchester Met. We are one of the UK's leading modern universities for research quality, and our research delivers real-world impact locally, nationally and internationally. About the Role Working closely with the Principal Investigator, academic project team and professional services colleagues, you will provide project management and coordination support to ensure the successful delivery of the BeST Engage project. You will play a key role in supporting project governance, monitoring progress against milestones and ensuring compliance with funder requirements. Acting as a central point of coordination, you will support communication across project partners and stakeholder groups, helping to maintain effective working relationships throughout the life of the project. Your responsibilities will include: Coordinating project meetings and governance activities. Supporting the monitoring of project finances and expenditure. Maintaining project records, documentation and reporting schedules. Coordinating reporting and monitoring activity across project work packages. Supporting engagement with project partners, stakeholders and the funder. Working with colleagues across the University to ensure compliance with contractual, governance and funding requirements. Identifying and escalating risks, issues and actions as appropriate. This role offers an excellent opportunity to gain experience of managing a major externally funded research project and working within a collaborative research environment. About You You will have experience of working in a project support, project management or administrative role, with the ability to coordinate multiple activities and stakeholders simultaneously. You will also have: Excellent organisational and planning skills, with the ability to manage competing priorities and meet deadlines. Strong communication and interpersonal skills. Experience of organising meetings, maintaining records and tracking actions. Good numerical and analytical skills, with experience of monitoring budgets or financial information. The ability to work effectively with a wide range of internal and external stakeholders. Strong attention to detail and a commitment to delivering a high-quality service. The ability to work independently whilst contributing positively as part of a team. Experience of working within a higher education, research or externally funded project environment would be advantageous but is not essential. Working at Manchester Met Manchester Met offers a fantastic range of benefits to employees, including: Central location with excellent transport links. Generous annual leave allowance. Competitive pension scheme. Access to retail discounts. Employee Assistance Programme. Cycle to Work scheme. A wide range of health and wellbeing initiatives. Various other rewards and benefits. How to Apply Your application must include a supporting statement demonstrating how your skills and experience meet the requirements outlined in the Person Specification, together with an up-to-date Curriculum Vitae. For an informal discussion about the role, please contact Amy Clow, Faculty Research & Innovation Manager , at A.Clow@mmu.ac.uk . Manchester Metropolitan University is committed to supporting the rights, responsibilities, dignity, health and wellbeing of staff and students through our commitment to equality, diversity and inclusion. We welcome applications from all sections of the community, irrespective of background, belief or identity, recognising the benefits that a diverse workforce brings to our University. We particularly encourage applications from groups that are currently underrepresented within our workforce. Hybrid working is offered for this role. The nature of the role requires a regular on-campus presence, although some activities can be undertaken remotely. We recognise the benefits and importance of flexible working and welcome conversations about this throughout the recruitment process. Documents Job Description.pdf (243.38 KB) Candidate Pack.pdf (9.15 MB) Apply Now Apply Now Details Location: Manchester Birley Campus Faculty / Function: Research & Innovation Salary: Grade 6 (£31,236 to £34,610) pro rata Closing Date: 12 October 2026 Contract Type: Fixed Term Contract Length: 30 June 2028 Contracted Hours per week: 18.5 Benefits 25 days leave + Christmas closure + Bank holidays (Extra 5 days after 5 years of service) Travel loan Wellbeing platform Life insurance Access to Campus Facilities Enhanced parental leave High-quality guaranteed pension Meet the recruiter Michelle Legg ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk Loading Start at the next stage of your career Find out more about our opportunities, or get in touch to discuss bringing your expertise to a university where you'll be supported and valued. Explore our vacancies Get in touch Get in touch Manchester Metropolitan University All Saints Building Manchester M15 6BH United Kingdom ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk +44 (0)161 247 6820 Facebook icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Facebook Twitter icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Twitter YouTube icon Manchester Metropolitan University on YouTube LinkedIn icon Manchester Metropolitan University on LinkedIn Instagram icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Instagram Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply About us Search Get in touch Policies, regulations and legal notices Cookies Website terms of use Accessibility Freedom of information Governance of the University Modern slavery © 2026 Manchester Metropolitan University, all rights reserved. Cookie Preferences This site uses cookies and other tracking technologies to improve your browsing experience, show personalised content/ads and analyse site traffic. Select cookies to accept Required cookies These cookies are used to ensure the user has a secure journey through the site. earcusessionid - Used to maintain your session. earcusession - Used to secure your session. earcucc - Used to manage your cookie preferences. Analytics Cookies Analytics cookies or performance cookies are used to track website visitors and their user behaviour. _ga - Used by Google Analytics. _gid - Used by Google Analytics. _gat - Used by Google Analytics. _fbp - Used by Meta (Facebook) Pixel. Accept Cookies Accept All Cookies Customise Cookies Reject All Optional"
