    "https://manmetjobs.mmu.ac.uk/jobs/vacancy/research-degrees-administrator-9526-manchester-all-saints-campus/9423/description/": {
      "title": "Research Degrees Administrator",
      "description": "Research Degrees Administrator - (9526) | Manchester Metropolitan University Careers CareerZone - Research Degrees Administrator (9526) Open toolbar Accessibility Grayscale High contrast Negative contrast Light background Links underline Readable font Reset Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Research Degrees Administrator - (9526) The Doctoral College at Manchester Metropolitan University is home to a vibrant community of doctoral students whose work drives world-leading research and innovation. We are seeking an organised, proactive and customer-focused Research Degrees Administrator to join our Doctoral Services team and help deliver an outstanding experience for doctoral students, academic colleagues and external partners. About the Role As part of a supportive and collaborative team, you will play a key role in the effective administration of research degree programmes. Working closely with academic and professional services colleagues, you will help ensure processes are delivered efficiently, accurately and in line with University regulations. Key responsibilities include: Managing enquiries from doctoral students, academic staff and other stakeholders, providing clear and timely advice and guidance. Supporting administrative processes throughout the doctoral student lifecycle. Maintaining accurate student records and contributing to statutory and institutional reporting. Providing support for committees, quality assurance activities and performance monitoring. Contributing to the continuous improvement of systems, procedures and services within Doctoral Services. About the Team Doctoral Services sits within the Research and Innovation Directorate and provides specialist support for doctoral students and academic colleagues across the University. The team plays a vital role in delivering an excellent doctoral student experience while ensuring compliance, quality assurance and effective programme administration. You will join a friendly and experienced team that values collaboration, innovation and excellent service delivery. About You We are looking for a confident administrator with excellent organisational and communication skills, who enjoys working in a busy environment and managing a varied workload. You will have: Experience working in an administrative role involving complex processes and procedures. Experience providing information, advice and guidance while ensuring compliance with policies, regulations or established procedures. Strong organisational skills and the ability to manage competing priorities and meet deadlines. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with the confidence to build effective working relationships. Good digital skills, including experience of Microsoft Office applications and the ability to learn new systems quickly. A proactive, flexible and collaborative approach. A commitment to excellent customer service and continuous improvement. Please refer to the Person Specification within the Job Description for the full list of essential criteria. Why Join Manchester Met? Manchester Metropolitan University is an ambitious and inclusive institution with a strong commitment to research excellence, education and social impact. We offer a supportive working environment, opportunities for professional development and a comprehensive range of staff benefits. This is an excellent opportunity to build your career within a professional service that makes a meaningful contribution to the success of our doctoral research community. Are you a highly organised administrator who enjoys delivering excellent service and supporting complex processes? Then we would love to hear from you. Information for Applicants If you have any questions about the role please contact Hannah Shaw, Research Degrees Manager at h.shaw@mmu.ac.uk. To apply, please submit your CV and a covering letter outlining how you meet the criteria set out in the Job Description and Person Specification via the online portal. Manchester Metropolitan University is committed to equality, diversity and inclusion. We welcome applications from all backgrounds and particularly encourage applications from groups currently underrepresented within our workforce. We are also committed to supporting flexible working and welcome conversations about this throughout the recruitment process. Documents Job Description.pdf (295.28 KB) Candidate Pack.pdf (9.15 MB) Apply Now Apply Now Details Location: Manchester All Saints Campus Faculty / Function: Research & Innovation Salary: Grade 4 (£26,093 to £27,319) Closing Date: 12 October 2026 Contract Type: Permanent Contracted Hours per week: 35 Benefits 25 days leave + Christmas closure + Bank holidays (Extra 5 days after 5 years of service) Travel loan Wellbeing platform Life insurance Access to Campus Facilities Enhanced parental leave High-quality guaranteed pension Hybrid working opportunities Meet the recruiter Michelle Legg ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk Loading Start at the next stage of your career Find out more about our opportunities, or get in touch to discuss bringing your expertise to a university where you'll be supported and valued. Explore our vacancies Get in touch Get in touch Manchester Metropolitan University All Saints Building Manchester M15 6BH United Kingdom ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk +44 (0)161 247 6820 Facebook icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Facebook Twitter icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Twitter YouTube icon Manchester Metropolitan University on YouTube LinkedIn icon Manchester Metropolitan University on LinkedIn Instagram icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Instagram Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply About us Search Get in touch Policies, regulations and legal notices Cookies