    "https://manmetjobs.mmu.ac.uk/jobs/vacancy/programme-support-tutor-9477-manchester-birley-campus/9376/description/": {
      "title": "Programme Support Tutor",
      "description": "Programme Support Tutor - (9477) | Manchester Metropolitan University Careers CareerZone - Programme Support Tutor (9477) Open toolbar Accessibility Grayscale High contrast Negative contrast Light background Links underline Readable font Reset Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Programme Support Tutor - (9477) The School of Psychology is looking for an organised, proactive and student-focused Programme Support Tutor to join our team. This is a varied role that sits at the heart of our programme delivery, working closely with the Head of School, Associate Heads and Programme Coordinators to ensure our programmes run smoothly and our students receive a positive and supportive experience. You'll provide a combination of programme administration, student support and teaching and learning support. From helping with admissions and recruitment activities, to coordinating timetables and academic calendars, supporting assessment and learning resources, and responding to issues that affect the student experience, you'll play an important role in the day-to-day operation and continued development of our programmes. There will also be opportunities to contribute to teaching, provide cover when required and support students with their studies, assessments and progression. What you'll be doing You'll have a broad and varied remit, including: Supporting recruitment, selection and admissions activity, including Open Days and Visit Days. Working with Programme Coordinators and Associate Heads to support effective timetabling and programme scheduling. Helping to develop and maintain programme calendars, assessment dates and other key activities. Supporting the development and organisation of learning resources and teaching materials. Contributing to the development of assessments and exam materials as directed by academic colleagues. Supporting alternative teaching arrangements when staff absence affects programme delivery. Using a range of creative and engaging teaching approaches, including online and blended learning, when delivering teaching. Supporting students to understand assessment requirements, prepare for examinations and develop their academic and transferable skills. Providing advice and guidance to students, referring them to specialist University services where appropriate. Analysing attendance and performance data and using this to help improve student engagement, retention, performance and progression. Producing reports and information for Programme Leaders, Programme Committees and senior colleagues. Supporting student induction and transition into higher education. Coordinating student events and initiating projects in response to identified needs. Working collaboratively with colleagues across the University, including Student Services, the Students' Union, Library, IT and programme administration teams. About you We're looking for someone who is confident working with both academic colleagues and students and who can manage a varied workload with initiative and enthusiasm. You'll need excellent communication skills, with the ability to explain complex information clearly both verbally and in writing. You'll be able to work independently while also being a strong team player, and you'll have the judgement and creativity to respond effectively when programme or student issues arise. You'll have experience of supporting programmes in a higher education environment, together with knowledge of University systems and processes. Experience of teaching, student support, scheduling or working with online and blended learning would be an advantage. A degree or equivalent qualification, together with evidence of continuing professional development, is essential. Above all, we're looking for someone who is committed to providing a high standard of service and who genuinely cares about creating a positive student experience. To apply: Please attach your CV and covering letter to the online portal. Manchester Metropolitan University fosters an inclusive culture of belonging that promotes equity and celebrates diversity. We value a diverse workforce for the innovation and diversity of thought it brings and welcome applications from all local and international communities, including Black, Asian, and Minority Ethnic backgrounds, disabled people, and LGBTQ+ individuals. We support a range of flexible working arrangements, including hybrid and tailored schedules, which can be discussed with your line manager. If you require reasonable adjustments during the recruitment process or in your role, please let us know so we can provide appropriate support. Our commitment to inclusivity includes mentoring programmes, accessibility resources, and professional development opportunities to empower and support underrepresented groups. Manchester Met is a Disability Confident Leader and, under this scheme, aims to offer an interview to disabled people who apply for the role and meet the essential criteria as listed in the attached Job Description for that vacancy. This vacancy is expected to attract a high volume of applications. Therefore, under the Disability Confident Scheme, only disabled people who apply under the scheme and best meet the essential criteria will be offered an interview. Documents Job Description.pdf (290.93 KB) Candidate Pack.pdf (9.15 MB) Apply Now Apply Now Details Location: Manchester Birley Campus Faculty / Function: Health & Education Salary: Grade 7 (£35,608 to £39,906) Closing Date: 13 October 2026 Contract Type: Permanent Contracted Hours per week: 35 Benefits Meet the recruiter Michelle Legg ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk Loading Start at the next stage of your career Find out more about our opportunities, or get in touch to discuss bringing your expertise to a university where you'll be supported and valued. Explore our vacancies Get in touch Get in touch Manchester Metropolitan University All Saints Building Manchester M15 6BH United Kingdom ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk +44 (0)161 247 6820 Facebook icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Facebook Twitter icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Twitter YouTube icon Manchester Metropolitan University on YouTube LinkedIn icon Manchester Metropolitan University on LinkedIn Instagram icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Instagram Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply About us Search Get in touch Policies, regulations and legal notices Cookies Website terms of use Accessibility Freedom of information Governance of the University Modern slavery © 2026 Manchester Metropolitan University, all rights reserved. Cookie Preferences This site uses cookies and other tracking technologies to improve your browsing experience, show personalised content/ads and analyse site traffic. Select cookies to accept Required cookies These cookies are used to ensure the user has a secure journey through the site. earcusessionid - Used to maintain your session. earcusession - Used to secure your session. earcucc - Used to manage your cookie preferences. Analytics Cookies Analytics cookies or performance cookies are used to track website visitors and their user behaviour. _ga - Used by Google Analytics. _gid - Used by Google Analytics. _gat - Used by Google Analytics. _fbp - Used by Meta (Facebook) Pixel. Accept Cookies Accept All Cookies Customise Cookies Reject All Optional"
