    "https://manmetjobs.mmu.ac.uk/jobs/vacancy/research-associate-in-microfluidic-diagnostics-9479-manchester-all-saints-campus/9378/description/": {
      "title": "Research Associate in Microfluidic Diagnostics -",
      "description": "Research Associate in Microfluidic Diagnostics - (9479) | Manchester Metropolitan University Careers CareerZone - Research Associate in Microfluidic Diagnostics (9479) Open toolbar Accessibility Grayscale High contrast Negative contrast Light background Links underline Readable font Reset Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Research Associate in Microfluidic Diagnostics - (9479) About the Faculty Manchester Metropolitan University is one of the UK's largest and most popular universities — and in August 2026, we're launching something truly exciting. Our brand‑new School of Biological and Chemical Sciences will unite our existing strengths across biomedical science, human physiology, biomedicine, clinical science, microbiology, biology, zoology, medicinal and pharmaceutical chemistry, and chemistry. This is a rare chance to join us right at the start of this new chapter. About the Department You'll be part of a vibrant, forward‑thinking School designed to spark collaboration, drive innovation, and open up new opportunities for our students and staff. Based within the Faculty of Science and Engineering, you'll benefit from modern, spacious, and well‑equipped teaching and research facilities . About the Project You will be working as part of a UKDI funded project developing portable clinical diagnostics for deployment in extreme environments alongside Dr Kirsty Shaw. Dr Kirsty Shaw | Manchester Metropolitan University About the Role & Team You will be part of a collaborative project between Manchester Metropolitan University and StreamBio. Based in the Dalton Building, you will work closely alongside the academic lead for the project, Dr Kirsty Shaw, but will also regularly exchange findings and expertise with industrial colleagues. About You You will be responsible for the development of new microfluidic devices for blood typing and detection of bloodborne viruses in remote locations. The successful candidate will have experience in microfluidics and/or molecular biology. They will be able to demonstrate independent research experience, alongside excellent team-working and be willing to participate in an industry-led project. To learn more about role and requirements, please read the Job Description provided below. Application & Assessment Process: To apply, please submit a CV and covering letter detailing your suitability, on the application portal. For informal enquiries, about this vacancy, please contact Dr Kirsty Shaw on k.shaw@mmu.ac.uk Please be aware that only applications including a cover letter may be considered at shortlisting stage. Interviews will be held on 23 October. Please note additional requirements and background checks on the successful individual may be required by the industrial partner. We believe in working together, sharing knowledge and valuing everyone's contributions. Develop your skills, further your knowledge and be part of a team who are transforming lives, every single day! Manchester Metropolitan University fosters an inclusive culture of belonging that promotes equity and celebrates diversity. We value a diverse workforce for the innovation and diversity of thought it brings and welcome applications from local and international communities, including those from Black, Asian, and Minority Ethnic backgrounds, disabled people, and LGBTQ+ individuals. We support a range of flexible working arrangements, including hybrid and tailored schedules, which can be discussed with your line manager. If you require reasonable adjustments during the recruitment process or in your role, please let us know so we can provide appropriate support. Our commitment to inclusivity includes mentoring programmes, accessibility resources, and professional development opportunities to empower and support underrepresented groups. Manchester Met is a Disability Confident Leader and, under this scheme, aims to offer an interview to disabled people who apply for the role and meet the essential criteria as listed in the attached Job Description for that vacancy. Documents 000213.1 Research Associate Grade 7 - JD.pdf (71.27 KB) Apply Now Apply Now Details Location: Manchester All Saints Campus Faculty / Function: Science & Engineering Salary: Grade 7 (£36,320 to £40,704) Closing Date: 13 October 2026 Contract Type: Fixed Term Contract Length: 07/03/2028 Contracted Hours per week: 35 Benefits 25 days leave + Christmas closure + Bank holidays (Extra 5 days after 5 years of service) Travel loan Wellbeing platform Life insurance Access to Campus Facilities Enhanced parental leave High-quality guaranteed pension Meet the recruiter Neha Phanse ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk Loading Start at the next stage of your career Find out more about our opportunities, or get in touch to discuss bringing your expertise to a university where you'll be supported and valued. Explore our vacancies Get in touch Get in touch Manchester Metropolitan University All Saints Building Manchester M15 6BH United Kingdom ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk +44 (0)161 247 6820 Facebook icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Facebook Twitter icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Twitter YouTube icon Manchester Metropolitan University on YouTube LinkedIn icon Manchester Metropolitan University on LinkedIn Instagram icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Instagram Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply About us Search Get in touch Policies, regulations and legal notices Cookies Website terms of use Accessibility Freedom of information Governance of the University Modern slavery © 2026 Manchester Metropolitan University, all rights reserved."
    },
    "https://manmetjobs.mmu.ac.uk/jobs/vacancy/student-transition-and-transformation-manager-student-services-9476-manchester-all-saints-campus/9375/description/": {
      "title": "Student Transition and Transformation Manager Student Services",
      "description": "Student Transition and Transformation Manager Student Services - (9476) | Manchester Metropolitan University Careers CareerZone - Student Transition and Transformation Manager Student Services (9476) Open toolbar Accessibility Grayscale High contrast Negative contrast Light background Links underline Readable font Reset Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Student Transition and Transformation Manager Student Services - (9476) Are you passionate about creating exceptional student experiences and driving meaningful change at scale? This is an exciting opportunity to shape how students engage with our services throughout their university journey and lead transformational projects that make a genuine difference to student outcomes. As Student Experience and Transformation Manager, you'll play a pivotal role in driving strategic change across Student Services, helping to ensure that all interactions students have with us are connected, accessible and impactful. About the role: As part of the Student Services Leadership Team, you'll play a leading role in shaping and enhancing the student experience across Manchester Met. Working collaboratively with colleagues across Academic and Professional Services, you'll turn insight into action, ensuring our services support students effectively from application through to graduation. In this role, you will: Lead strategic student experience and transformation projects that deliver meaningful improvements for students. Drive initiatives focused on student engagement, transition, belonging, retention and success. Develop approaches that strengthen the student voice and ensure feedback informs decision-making and service development. Use data, insight and evaluation to identify opportunities, measure impact and support continuous improvement. Build strong partnerships across the University, Students' Union and external stakeholders to deliver joined-up, student-centred services. Champion inclusive practice and targeted interventions that improve outcomes for underrepresented student groups. This is a highly visible role that offers the opportunity to influence institutional priorities, work closely with senior stakeholders and lead initiatives that make a lasting difference to the student experience across the University. We offer a competitive benefits package including generous annual leave, excellent pension provision, access to wellbeing support, family-friendly policies, ongoing professional development opportunities and a range of staff benefits and discounts. About you: We're looking for an experienced and influential professional who is passionate about enhancing the student experience and driving positive change. You will bring: Significant experience of leading large-scale student experience, engagement or transformation projects within a complex organisation. Strong project management skills, with the ability to coordinate multiple priorities and deliver measurable outcomes. Excellent stakeholder engagement skills and the confidence to influence and collaborate at both operational and senior leadership levels. Experience of using data, insight and feedback to identify opportunities, evaluate impact and inform strategic decisions. A strong understanding of the higher education sector, student needs and the factors that contribute to student success, engagement and belonging. A commitment to inclusive practice and creating opportunities for all students to thrive. Most importantly, you'll be someone who can bring people together around a shared vision and turn ideas into tangible improvements that enhance students' lives. How to apply: Ready to help shape the future of Student Services at Manchester Met? We'd love to hear from you! To apply, please click “Apply Now” , complete the pre-screening questions and upload your CV and Cover Letter outlining your suitability to the role. Your cover letter should be no more than 2 pages max. Please review the job description and person specification (attached below) carefully before applying and demonstrate how you meet the essential criteria within your application. For informal enquiries about the role, please contact Jenny Clough, Director of Student Services, via J.Clough@mmu.ac.uk . Please note: Interviews are provisonally scheduled to take place 03 November (03/11/26) Further information: Manchester Metropolitan University fosters an inclusive culture of belonging that promotes equity and celebrates diversity. We value a diverse workforce for the innovation and diversity of thought it brings and welcome applications from all local and international communities, including Black, Asian, and Minority Ethnic backgrounds, disabled people, and LGBTQ+ individuals. We support a range of flexible working arrangements, including hybrid and tailored schedules, which can be discussed with your line manager. If you require reasonable adjustments during the recruitment process or in your role, please let us know so we can provide appropriate support. Our commitment to inclusivity includes mentoring programmes, accessibility resources, and professional development opportunities to empower and support underrepresented groups. Manchester Met is a Disability Confident Leader and, under this scheme, aims to offer an interview to disabled people who apply for the role and meet the essential criteria as listed in the attached Job Description for that vacancy. Documents 002504.1 Student Experience and Transformation Manager.pdf (133.36 KB) Candidate Pack.pdf (9.16 MB) Apply Now Apply Now Details Location: Manchester All Saints Campus Faculty / Function: Academic Services Salary: Grade 9 (£48,822 to £56,535) Closing Date: 13 October 2026 Contract Type: Permanent Contracted Hours per week: 37 Benefits 35 days leave + Christmas closure + Bank holidays Travel loan Wellbeing platform Life insurance Access to Campus Facilities Enhanced parental leave High-quality guaranteed pension Hybrid working opportunities Meet the recruiter Claire Muir ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk Loading Start at the next stage of your career Find out more about our opportunities, or get in touch to discuss bringing your expertise to a university where you'll be supported and valued. Explore our vacancies Get in touch Get in touch Manchester Metropolitan University All Saints Building Manchester M15 6BH United Kingdom ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk +44 (0)161 247 6820 Facebook icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Facebook Twitter icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Twitter YouTube icon Manchester Metropolitan University on YouTube LinkedIn icon Manchester Metropolitan University on LinkedIn Instagram icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Instagram Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply About us Search Get in touch Policies, regulations and legal notices Cookies Website terms of use Accessibility Freedom of information Governance of the University Modern slavery © 2026 Manchester Metropolitan University, all rights reserved. Cookie Preferences This site uses cookies and other tracking technologies to improve your browsing experience, show personalised content/ads and analyse site traffic. Select cookies to accept Required cookies These cookies are used to ensure the user has a secure journey through the site. earcusessionid - Used to maintain your session. earcusession - Used to secure your session. earcucc - Used to manage your cookie preferences. Analytics Cookies Analytics cookies or performance cookies are used to track website visitors and their user behaviour. _ga - Used by Google Analytics. _gid - Used by Google Analytics. _gat - Used by Google Analytics. _fbp - Used by Meta (Facebook) Pixel. Accept Cookies Accept All Cookies Customise Cookies Reject All Optional"
    },
    "https://manmetjobs.mmu.ac.uk/jobs/vacancy/campus-security-officer-9529-other/9426/description/": {
      "title": "Campus Security Officer",
      "description": "Campus Security Officer - (9529) | Manchester Metropolitan University Careers CareerZone - Campus Security Officer (9529) Open toolbar Accessibility Grayscale High contrast Negative contrast Light background Links underline Readable font Reset Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Campus Security Officer - (9529) Are you someone who stays calm under pressure, enjoys helping others and takes pride in delivering exceptional customer service? Join a team that plays a vital role in keeping our University community safe, supported and secure, responding to a wide range of situations with professionalism, care and confidence. About the team or project: Manchester Met University Security service is an exceptional service carried out with pride and professionalism. This is provided by 4 teams covering the security role 24/7. Each team has a supervisor and a duty manager reporting into the CSOM who then reports up to the HoS. The security team provide first response to all security incidents that occur across the MMU footprint including and not restricted to; First aid requests, Building lockdown and unlocking, Supporting events, report writing, investigating, welfare support among many others. About the role: Although the post is security related, we are not necessarily seeking individuals with experience in the sector, our preference being to employ someone with the right customer ethos and experience of working within teams delivering first class customer care. One of the most important roles this post incorporates is that of first response to emergencies, safety and welfare related incidents and as such, we are looking for an individual who is calm under pressure, caring and compassionate. Reporting to the Campus Security Supervisor at the start of each shift, you will be given a brief on the expectations for the tasks for the shift and zone,  deployed to your allocated zone to be able to respond to any security related task using your own initiative and skills to ensure the best service is provided to all stakeholders. About you: We're looking for enthusiastic and proactive colleagues who will help us continue to develop and enhance our security service. You'll be able to demonstrate: Excellent communication and interpersonal skills A strong commitment to customer service and supporting others The ability to remain calm and professional under pressure Strong organisational skills and the ability to prioritise workload effectively Ownership and accountability for your responsibilities/workloads The confidence to use your initiative and make informed decisions The ability to lead, motivate and support colleagues when required A collaborative approach to working as part of a team and across the wider University community To apply: Please click 'Apply Now' to submit your application through our online recruitment system. As part of your application, please upload a CV and a covering letter that clearly demonstrates how you meet the essential criteria outlined in the job description. Applications must be submitted via the online system. Further information: Manchester Metropolitan University fosters an inclusive culture of belonging that promotes equity and celebrates diversity. We value a diverse workforce for the innovation and diversity of thought it brings and welcome applications from all local and international communities, including Black, Asian, and Minority Ethnic backgrounds, disabled people, and LGBTQ+ individuals. We support a range of flexible working arrangements, including hybrid and tailored schedules, which can be discussed with your line manager. If you require reasonable adjustments during the recruitment process or in your role, please let us know so we can provide appropriate support. Our commitment to inclusivity includes mentoring programmes, accessibility resources, and professional development opportunities to empower and support underrepresented groups. Manchester Met is a Disability Confident Leader and, under this scheme, aims to offer an interview to disabled people who apply for the role and meet the essential criteria as listed in the attached Job Description for that vacancy. Documents Campus Security Officer Job Description.pdf (71.51 KB) Candidate Pack.pdf (9.16 MB) Apply Now Apply Now Details Location: Other Faculty / Function: Estates, Facilities and Campus Development Salary: Grade 4 (£26,093 to £27,319) Closing Date: 14 October 2026 Contract Type: Permanent Contracted Hours per week: 35 Benefits 25 days leave + Christmas closure + Bank holidays (Extra 5 days after 5 years of service) Travel loan Wellbeing platform Life insurance Access to Campus Facilities Enhanced parental leave High-quality guaranteed pension Meet the recruiter Claire Muir ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk Loading Start at the next stage of your career Find out more about our opportunities, or get in touch to discuss bringing your expertise to a university where you'll be supported and valued. Explore our vacancies Get in touch Get in touch Manchester Metropolitan University All Saints Building Manchester M15 6BH United Kingdom ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk +44 (0)161 247 6820 Facebook icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Facebook Twitter icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Twitter YouTube icon Manchester Metropolitan University on YouTube LinkedIn icon Manchester Metropolitan University on LinkedIn Instagram icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Instagram Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply About us Search Get in touch Policies, regulations and legal notices Cookies Website terms of use Accessibility Freedom of information Governance of the University Modern slavery © 2026 Manchester Metropolitan University, all rights reserved. Cookie Preferences This site uses cookies and other tracking technologies to improve your browsing experience, show personalised content/ads and analyse site traffic. Select cookies to accept Required cookies These cookies are used to ensure the user has a secure journey through the site. earcusessionid - Used to maintain your session. earcusession - Used to secure your session. earcucc - Used to manage your cookie preferences. Analytics Cookies Analytics cookies or performance cookies are used to track website visitors and their user behaviour. _ga - Used by Google Analytics. _gid - Used by Google Analytics. _gat - Used by Google Analytics. _fbp - Used by Meta (Facebook) Pixel. Accept Cookies Accept All Cookies Customise Cookies Reject All Optional"
