    "https://manmetjobs.mmu.ac.uk/jobs/vacancy/education-services-administrator-assessment-management-9464-manchester-all-saints-campus/9363/description/": {
      "title": "Education Services Administrator (Assessment Management)",
      "description": "Education Services Administrator (Assessment Management) - (9464) | Manchester Metropolitan University Careers CareerZone - Education Services Administrator (Assessment Management) (9464) Open toolbar Accessibility Grayscale High contrast Negative contrast Light background Links underline Readable font Reset Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Education Services Administrator (Assessment Management) - (9464) Do you want to work for one of the UK's top three sustainable Universities? Are you passionate about helping people and have an aptitude for customer service and communication? See this exciting and rewarding opportunity to join Manchester Metropolitan University and become a valued member of the Assessment Management department! How to apply: Please ensure that you include a CV and a detailed covering letter with your application. Shortlisting is carried out based on your covering letter and you should be clear about how you meet each of the Person Specification criteria, and give evidence of your experience. Please number your points in line with the corresponding Person Specification requirement. All staff in Education Services have generic job titles and descriptions, in this case Education Services Administrator, but we welcome applications from a broad range of stakeholder/customer services backgrounds. About the role: We are recruiting an Education Services Administrator in the Assessment Management department. Education Services Administrators are responsible for completing key foundational tasks, enabling the smooth functioning of the department. Administrators can work independently on tasks and occasionally work with colleagues across teams on projects, to achieve the wider goals of the department. Specific tasks vary depending on teams but include general administrative duties, such as answering stakeholder enquiries and looking into student records and handling data by using the University systems. About the Assessment Management department: Assessment is at the heart of what a university does, and our department's purpose is to enable our students and colleagues to achieve their best by delivering sector-leading excellence and innovation in assessment management. Consisting of seven teams, Assessment Management work in a positive environment which encourages the development of skills and professional growth. All roles are varied, but a brief flavour of the core work of each team is listed below. Our teams: Assessment Delivery – organising and scheduling exams, set-up and receipt of coursework. Assessment Systems – configuration of assessment-related systems, including the configuration of progression rules, data manipulation and interrogation. Assessment Standards – oversight of regulations, quality processes, external examining, and academic misconduct. Assessment Service Desk – first line stakeholder support, triaging queries via a ticketing system, phone calls and email. The role would suit someone with a passion for delivering customer service. Assessment Results – managing student assessment records, ensuring marks are present and correct, and student results are published in a timely fashion via the running of assessment boards. Assessment Mitigations – oversight of student extensions and finding ways to ensure students who experience difficulties have the best possible chance of continuing their studies. Roles are based within particular teams; however, colleagues work collaboratively and flexibly to support the needs of the whole department in relation to the demands of the academic calendar. We have a standard induction period and a buddy system to enable new starters to smoothly settle into the department. Ideal candidate: Our colleagues in Assessment Management say below are the key traits to be a successful Education Services Administrator: ‘ Flexible, conscientious, responsible' ‘Team player, good communication, problem solving' ‘Ability to adapt, calm, focused' For more detailed requirements of the role, please check the Person Specification attached to this job advert. From our colleagues: See what some of our team members had to say when asked what their favourite thing is about working in Assessment Management! ‘ The people are incredibly supportive! ' ‘ The team are fantastic to work with and it's a very supportive environment with plenty of opportunities to learn and develop skills.' ‘I love working with a friendly team, everyone is so supportive!' For an informal discussion about the role, please contact: Hana Lee, H.Lee@mmu.ac.uk , Service Development and Innovation Manager. Further information: Manchester Metropolitan University fosters an inclusive culture of belonging that promotes equity and celebrates diversity. We value a diverse workforce for the innovation and diversity of thought it brings and welcome applications from all local and international communities, including Black, Asian, and Minority Ethnic backgrounds, disabled people, and LGBTQ+ individuals. We support a range of flexible working arrangements, including hybrid and tailored schedules, which can be discussed with your line manager. If you require reasonable adjustments during the recruitment process or in your role, please let us know so we can provide appropriate support. Our commitment to inclusivity includes mentoring programmes, accessibility resources, and professional development opportunities to empower and support underrepresented groups. Manchester Met is a Disability Confident Leader and, under this scheme, aims to offer an interview to disabled people who apply for the role and meet the essential criteria as listed in the attached Job Description for that vacancy. This vacancy is expected to attract a high volume of applications. Therefore, under the Disability Confident Scheme, only disabled people who apply under the scheme and best meet the essential criteria will be offered an interview. Documents 001089.2 G4 Education Services Administrator.pdf (70.16 KB) Candidate Pack.pdf (9.16 MB) Apply Now Apply Now Details Location: Manchester All Saints Campus Faculty / Function: Academic Services Salary: Grade 4 (£26,093 to £27,319) Closing Date: 14 October 2026 Contract Type: Permanent Contracted Hours per week: 35 Benefits 25 days leave + Christmas closure + Bank holidays (Extra 5 days after 5 years of service) Travel loan Wellbeing platform Life insurance Access to Campus Facilities Enhanced parental leave High-quality guaranteed pension Hybrid working opportunities Meet the recruiter Claire Muir ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk Loading Start at the next stage of your career Find out more about our opportunities, or get in touch to discuss bringing your expertise to a university where you'll be supported and valued. Explore our vacancies Get in touch Get in touch Manchester Metropolitan University All Saints Building Manchester M15 6BH United Kingdom ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk +44 (0)161 247 6820 Facebook icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Facebook Twitter icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Twitter YouTube icon Manchester Metropolitan University on YouTube LinkedIn icon Manchester Metropolitan University on LinkedIn Instagram icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Instagram Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply About us Search Get in touch Policies, regulations and legal notices Cookies Website terms of use Accessibility Freedom of information Governance of the University Modern slavery © 2026 Manchester Metropolitan University, all rights reserved. Cookie Preferences This site uses cookies and other tracking technologies to improve your browsing experience, show personalised content/ads and analyse site traffic. Select cookies to accept Required cookies These cookies are used to ensure the user has a secure journey through the site. earcusessionid - Used to maintain your session. earcusession - Used to secure your session. earcucc - Used to manage your cookie preferences. Analytics Cookies Analytics cookies or performance cookies are used to track website visitors and their user behaviour. _ga - Used by Google Analytics. _gid - Used by Google Analytics. _gat - Used by Google Analytics. _fbp - Used by Meta (Facebook) Pixel. Accept Cookies Accept All Cookies Customise Cookies Reject All Optional"
    },
    "https://manmetjobs.mmu.ac.uk/jobs/vacancy/research-associate-in-education--9548-manchester-birley-campus/9444/description/": {
      "title": "Research Associate in Education -",
      "description": "Research Associate in Education  - (9548) | Manchester Metropolitan University Careers CareerZone - Research Associate in Education  (9548) Open toolbar Accessibility Grayscale High contrast Negative contrast Light background Links underline Readable font Reset Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Research Associate in Education  - (9548) The School of Education is looking for a Research Associate to join an exciting programme of research exploring the future of sustainable school leadership . Working with Professor Toby Greany and the wider research team , you will contribute to research examining how school leaders are responding to the changing demands being placed on schools, their staff, pupils and communities. The role will build on Professor Greany's recent ESRC-funded research into Sustainable School Leadership across the UK. The research highlighted how the COVID-19 pandemic acted as a significant turning point for schools, accelerating changes already underway while creating new challenges for school leaders. Alongside their focus on teaching, learning and educational improvement, leaders are increasingly required to respond to issues including inclusion, additional learning needs, mental health and wellbeing, safeguarding, behaviour and attendance. This has raised important questions about the purpose of education, the role of school leaders and how schools can create environments where both educational improvement and care are supported. About the role As Research Associate, you will play an important role in extending our understanding of these issues. You will undertake a range of research activities, including: conducting literature reviews and engaging with relevant academic and policy research planning and carrying out qualitative and/or quantitative research undertaking interviews, focus groups and surveys with school leaders and other stakeholders analysing and interpreting research data preparing research reports, papers and other outputs presenting findings to academic and professional audiences contributing to academic publications, conferences and seminars developing research partnerships and networks within the UK and internationally working with the research team to develop proposals for future large-scale research and funding opportunities. The project includes research across a selection of European countries, so there will also be opportunities for national and international travel and to develop your research networks beyond the UK. You will have the opportunity to take responsibility for aspects of the research project, while working closely with Professor Greany and other senior colleagues. You may also have opportunities to support research assistants and students and contribute to teaching-related activities within the School of Education. About you We are looking for someone with a strong interest in school leadership, education policy and the changing role of schools . You will have experience of undertaking research and be confident working with qualitative and/or quantitative research methods. You will be able to analyse complex information, identify key themes and communicate your findings clearly to different audiences. You will ideally have experience of research relating to school leadership and policy, together with evidence of making an independent contribution to research projects and producing written research outputs. You will also be able to demonstrate: experience of designing and undertaking research the ability to synthesise complex information from different sources strong written and verbal communication skills the ability to work independently, manage your own workload and meet deadlines an ability to work collaboratively as part of a research team a doctoral-level qualification, or evidence that you are currently working towards one. Experience of developing partnerships, presenting research, contributing to funding proposals or supporting student research would also be welcomed. Fluency in one or more European languages would be desirable. How to apply: Please attach your CV and covering letter to the online portal Interviews will take place on the 28th October Manchester Metropolitan University fosters an inclusive culture of belonging that promotes equity and celebrates diversity. We value a diverse workforce for the innovation and diversity of thought it brings and welcome applications from all local and international communities, including Black, Asian, and Minority Ethnic backgrounds, disabled people, and LGBTQ+ individuals. We support a range of flexible working arrangements, including hybrid and tailored schedules, which can be discussed with your line manager. If you require reasonable adjustments during the recruitment process or in your role, please let us know so we can provide appropriate support. Our commitment to inclusivity includes mentoring programmes, accessibility resources, and professional development opportunities to empower and support underrepresented groups. Manchester Met is a Disability Confident Leader and, under this scheme, aims to offer an interview to disabled people who apply for the role and meet the essential criteria as listed in the attached Job Description for that vacancy. Documents Job Description.pdf (262.36 KB) Candidate Pack.pdf (9.15 MB) Apply Now Apply Now Details Location: Manchester Birley Campus Faculty / Function: Health & Education Salary: Grade 7 (£35,608 to £39,906) Closing Date: 14 October 2026 Contract Type: Fixed Term Contract Length: 2 years Contracted Hours per week: 35 Benefits 25 days leave + Christmas closure + Bank holidays (Extra 5 days after 5 years of service) Travel loan Wellbeing platform Life insurance Access to Campus Facilities Enhanced parental leave High-quality guaranteed pension Meet the recruiter Michelle Legg ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk Loading Start at the next stage of your career Find out more about our opportunities, or get in touch to discuss bringing your expertise to a university where you'll be supported and valued. Explore our vacancies Get in touch Get in touch Manchester Metropolitan University All Saints Building Manchester M15 6BH United Kingdom ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk +44 (0)161 247 6820 Facebook icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Facebook Twitter icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Twitter YouTube icon Manchester Metropolitan University on YouTube LinkedIn icon Manchester Metropolitan University on LinkedIn Instagram icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Instagram Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply About us Search Get in touch Policies, regulations and legal notices Cookies Website terms of use Accessibility Freedom of information Governance of the University Modern slavery © 2026 Manchester Metropolitan University, all rights reserved."
    },
    "https://manmetjobs.mmu.ac.uk/jobs/vacancy/residential-services-manager-property-9489-manchester-birley-campus/9388/description/": {
      "title": "Residential Services Manager (Property)",
      "description": "Residential Services Manager (Property) - (9489) | Manchester Metropolitan University Careers CareerZone - Residential Services Manager (Property) (9489) Open toolbar Accessibility Grayscale High contrast Negative contrast Light background Links underline Readable font Reset Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Residential Services Manager (Property) - (9489) We are seeking an experienced and driven Residential Services Manager (Property) to join our Residential & Conference Services team. This is a fantastic opportunity for an operational leader with a passion for delivering exceptional customer experiences, managing complex property operations, and developing high-performing teams within a dynamic student accommodation environment. Reporting to the Head of Residential Services, you will play a key role in leading the University's residential property operations, ensuring the delivery of safe, compliant, customer-focused services while enhancing the student experience and supporting commercial growth opportunities. About the Role: As Residential Services Manager (Property), you will oversee the day-to-day management of University-owned residential properties, leading a multi-skilled operational team and driving service excellence across accommodation services. Your responsibilities will include: Leading, motivating and developing operational teams to deliver outstanding customer service and operational performance. Managing property operations, contractor performance and service delivery standards across residential accommodation. Ensuring compliance with all relevant health and safety legislation and the UUK Accommodation Code of Practice. Managing budgets, delivering value-for-money services and identifying opportunities for operational efficiencies. Supporting major projects, refurbishment programmes, residential conferences and commercial accommodation activities. Developing and implementing innovative processes and systems that enhance operational effectiveness and student satisfaction. Providing leadership during emergency situations and participating in the senior on-call rota. About you: We are looking for a confident and collaborative leader with significant operational management experience and a passion for delivering excellent customer outcomes. You will have: Essential Requirements Experience managing operational teams within a customer-focused environment. Strong leadership skills with the ability to motivate, coach and develop staff. Experience managing budgets and producing performance reports. In-depth knowledge of residential accommodation operations and associated health and safety requirements. IOSH or NEBOSH qualification. A degree (or equivalent professional experience) demonstrating strong analytical, literacy and numeracy skills. The ability to lead change, improve processes and drive continuous improvement. Desirable A recognised management qualification. Experience working within Higher Education or student accommodation. To apply: Please review the essential criteria within the job description, Click \"Apply Now\" and submit a CV and covering letter that clearly demonstrate your suitability for the role. For informal enquiries, please contact Martin Miller at m.miller@mmu.ac.uk Please note: Interviews are provisionally scheduled to take place on 27 October 2026 . Please ensure you are available on this date, as it may not be possible to accommodate requests for alternative interview dates. Further information: Manchester Metropolitan University fosters an inclusive culture of belonging that promotes equity and celebrates diversity. We value a diverse workforce for the innovation and diversity of thought it brings and welcome applications from all local and international communities, including Black, Asian, and Minority Ethnic backgrounds, disabled people, and LGBTQ+ individuals. We support a range of flexible working arrangements, including hybrid and tailored schedules, which can be discussed with your line manager. If you require reasonable adjustments during the recruitment process or in your role, please let us know so we can provide appropriate support. Our commitment to inclusivity includes mentoring programmes, accessibility resources, and professional development opportunities to empower and support underrepresented groups. Manchester Met is a Disability Confident Leader and, under this scheme, aims to offer an interview to disabled people who apply for the role and meet the essential criteria as listed in the attached Job Description for that vacancy. Documents Residential Services Manager (Property).pdf (258.76 KB) Candidate Pack.pdf (9.16 MB) Apply Now Apply Now Details Location: Manchester Birley Campus Faculty / Function: Estates, Facilities and Campus Development Salary: Grade 9 (£48,822 to £56,535) Closing Date: 14 October 2026 Contract Type: Fixed Term Contract Length: anticipated to end: 03/01/2028 Contracted Hours per week: 37 Benefits 35 days leave + Christmas closure + Bank holidays Travel loan Wellbeing platform Life insurance Access to Campus Facilities Enhanced parental leave High-quality guaranteed pension Meet the recruiter Claire Muir ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk Loading Start at the next stage of your career Find out more about our opportunities, or get in touch to discuss bringing your expertise to a university where you'll be supported and valued. Explore our vacancies Get in touch Get in touch Manchester Metropolitan University All Saints Building Manchester M15 6BH United Kingdom ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk +44 (0)161 247 6820 Facebook icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Facebook Twitter icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Twitter YouTube icon Manchester Metropolitan University on YouTube LinkedIn icon Manchester Metropolitan University on LinkedIn Instagram icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Instagram Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply About us Search Get in touch Policies, regulations and legal notices Cookies Website terms of use Accessibility Freedom of information Governance of the University Modern slavery © 2026 Manchester Metropolitan University, all rights reserved. Cookie Preferences This site uses cookies and other tracking technologies to improve your browsing experience, show personalised content/ads and analyse site traffic. Select cookies to accept Required cookies These cookies are used to ensure the user has a secure journey through the site. earcusessionid - Used to maintain your session. earcusession - Used to secure your session. earcucc - Used to manage your cookie preferences. Analytics Cookies Analytics cookies or performance cookies are used to track website visitors and their user behaviour. _ga - Used by Google Analytics. _gid - Used by Google Analytics. _gat - Used by Google Analytics. _fbp - Used by Meta (Facebook) Pixel. Accept Cookies Accept All Cookies Customise Cookies Reject All Optional"
    },
    "https://manmetjobs.mmu.ac.uk/jobs/vacancy/senior-operations-coordinator-student-engagement--experiential-learning-9505-manchester-all-saints-campus/9402/description/": {
      "title": "Senior Operations Coordinator (Student Engagement & Experiential Learning) -",
      "description": "Senior Operations Coordinator (Student Engagement & Experiential Learning) - (9505) | Manchester Metropolitan University Careers CareerZone - Senior Operations Coordinator (Student Engagement & Experiential Learning) (9505) Open toolbar Accessibility Grayscale High contrast Negative contrast Light background Links underline Readable font Reset Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Senior Operations Coordinator (Student Engagement & Experiential Learning) - (9505) Join a team helping students make the most of their university experience! At Manchester Metropolitan University, Rise, part of the Careers Service, helps students build skills, confidence and experience alongside their studies. Through projects, events, awards and other opportunities, Rise supports students to develop the skills employers value, explore their interests and make the most of their time at university. We're looking for a Senior Operations Coordinator to help our team deliver these opportunities successfully. This is a varied role combining project coordination, relationship-building, communications and service improvement. You'll work with colleagues across the University to help students access opportunities that support their personal and professional development. About the role: No two days are quite the same. You might be coordinating a student event, supporting a communications campaign, helping colleagues improve a process, responding to enquiries or working with academic staff to connect students with Rise opportunities. You'll help us: Coordinate projects, events and student development activities. Keep systems, processes and information up to date. Support communications and student engagement activity. Build positive working relationships with colleagues across the University. Monitor data and feedback to identify opportunities for improvement. Support the smooth running of financial, procurement and administrative processes. Help academic colleagues engage with experiential learning opportunities. About you: We're looking for someone who enjoys working with people and making things happen. You will be organised, adaptable and comfortable managing a range of activities at the same time. You'll enjoy finding practical solutions, improving ways of working and supporting colleagues to achieve shared goals. You'll be able to demonstrate: Experience coordinating projects, services or activities. Strong organisational and communication skills. An ability to build positive relationships with a wide range of people. Confidence using information and data to support decision-making. Good digital skills, including Microsoft 365. A commitment to providing an excellent experience for students and colleagues. Please see further information below regarding the application process, and the attached Job Description for further information on this role. Why Manchester Metropolitan? At Manchester Met you'll join a supportive and collaborative team that is passionate about helping students succeed. This role offers the opportunity to: Work with colleagues from across the University. Contribute to the continued development of Rise. Develop your own skills and experience. Help create opportunities that make a real difference to students. If you're excited by the opportunity to support students, work collaboratively and contribute to a service that has a positive impact across the University, we'd love to hear from you. To apply: To apply for this role, please click \"Apply Now\" and complete the online application process. As part of your application, you will first be required to complete five pre-screening questions based on the essential criteria outlined in the Job Description. Applicants must demonstrate experience in each of these areas to progress to the next stage of the application process. If successful at the pre-screening stage, you will then be asked to: Upload an up-to-date CV . Upload a covering letter of no more than one page explaining why you are the right person for this role and how your skills and experience meet the requirements of the post. Complete a short application question demonstrating your ability to coordinate operational activities, adapt to changing priorities, and maintain effective stakeholder relationships while delivering a high-quality service. We strongly recommend reviewing the Job Description and Person Specification before submitting your application, as these documents provide full details of the role requirements and selection criteria. Interview Information: Interviews are provisionally scheduled for 28 and 29 October 2026 . We recommend ensuring you are available on at least one of these dates before applying. Due to the availability of interview panels and the recruitment timetable, it may not be possible to offer alternative interview dates. Further information: Manchester Metropolitan University fosters an inclusive culture of belonging that promotes equity and celebrates diversity. We value a diverse workforce for the innovation and diversity of thought it brings and welcome applications from all local and international communities, including Black, Asian, and Minority Ethnic backgrounds, disabled people, and LGBTQ+ individuals. We support a range of flexible working arrangements, including hybrid and tailored schedules, which can be discussed with your line manager. If you require reasonable adjustments during the recruitment process or in your role, please let us know so we can provide appropriate support. Our commitment to inclusivity includes mentoring programmes, accessibility resources, and professional development opportunities to empower and support underrepresented groups. Manchester Met is a Disability Confident Leader and, under this scheme, aims to offer an interview to disabled people who apply for the role and meet the essential criteria as listed in the attached Job Description for that vacancy. Documents 002509.1 Rise Operations Coordinator.pdf (127.79 KB) Apply Now Apply Now Details Location: Manchester All Saints Campus Faculty / Function: Academic Services Salary: Grade 7 (£35,608 to £39,906) Closing Date: 14 October 2026 Contract Type: Permanent Contracted Hours per week: 35 Benefits 25 days leave + Christmas closure + Bank holidays (Extra 5 days after 5 years of service) Travel loan Wellbeing platform Life insurance Access to Campus Facilities Enhanced parental leave High-quality guaranteed pension Hybrid working opportunities Meet the recruiter Claire Muir ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk Loading Start at the next stage of your career Find out more about our opportunities, or get in touch to discuss bringing your expertise to a university where you'll be supported and valued. Explore our vacancies Get in touch Get in touch Manchester Metropolitan University All Saints Building Manchester M15 6BH United Kingdom ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk +44 (0)161 247 6820 Facebook icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Facebook Twitter icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Twitter YouTube icon Manchester Metropolitan University on YouTube LinkedIn icon Manchester Metropolitan University on LinkedIn Instagram icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Instagram Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply About us Search Get in touch Policies, regulations and legal notices Cookies Website terms of use Accessibility Freedom of information Governance of the University Modern slavery © 2026 Manchester Metropolitan University, all rights reserved."
    },
    "https://manmetjobs.mmu.ac.uk/jobs/vacancy/library-experience-coordinator-9532-manchester-all-saints-campus/9429/description/": {
      "title": "Library Experience Coordinator -",
      "description": "Library Experience Coordinator - (9532) | Manchester Metropolitan University Careers CareerZone - Library Experience Coordinator (9532) Open toolbar Accessibility Grayscale High contrast Negative contrast Light background Links underline Readable font Reset Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Library Experience Coordinator - (9532) Library Experience Coordinator Do you have experience of managing or supervising a team in a busy customer focused environment? Are you looking for a new challenge? Can you bring your skills and experience to a dynamic library setting? If you are a forward-thinking team leader who likes to drive innovation, loves developing team members, and has experience of creating a friendly and inclusive environment that thrives on excellent customer service, then our Library Experience Team could be the opportunity for you! About the Role As a Library Experience Co-ordinator, you will: Lead day-to-day service delivery and operational activity Respond positively and promptly to customer feedback and escalated complaints Manage and support Library Experience Advisers and Assistants to deliver excellent customer service both face-to-face and online Work collaboratively with other Library managers to plan and deliver projects that support organisational objectives This is a full-time permanent vacancy (35 hours per week). Evenings, weekend, and bank holiday working may be required. About you We are looking for someone who: Has experience delivering high-quality customer service and strong communication skills Has managed or supervised a team in a customer-facing environment Can identify and resolve day-to-day operational issues effectively Enjoys supporting and developing team members Further details can be found in the person specification section of the attached Job Description. We recognise that people may hesitate to apply unless they meet every requirement. If you are excited about the role and believe you can contribute, we encourage you to apply. To Apply: To apply, please upload your CV (no more than two sides). In lieu of a cover letter, you will be asked to complete three (3) mandatory application questions within the Supporting Information section. Once your CV has been uploaded, please proceed to the Supporting Information section to answer these questions. Shortlisted candidates will be invited to an interview and short assessment. Should you have any questions, please contact the hiring manager, Dayna Dawson, at d.dawson@mmu.ac.uk . Please note: Interviews are provisionally scheduled for 11 and 12 November 2026. As rescheduling may not be possible, we strongly encourage applicants to make a note of these dates before submitting their application. Further information: Manchester Metropolitan University fosters an inclusive culture of belonging that promotes equity and celebrates diversity. We value a diverse workforce for the innovation and diversity of thought it brings and welcome applications from all local and international communities, including Black, Asian, and Minority Ethnic backgrounds, disabled people, and LGBTQ+ individuals. We support a range of flexible working arrangements, including hybrid and tailored schedules, which can be discussed with your line manager. If you require reasonable adjustments during the recruitment process or in your role, please let us know so we can provide appropriate support. Our commitment to inclusivity includes mentoring programmes, accessibility resources, and professional development opportunities to empower and support underrepresented groups. Manchester Met is a Disability Confident Leader and, under this scheme, aims to offer an interview to disabled people who apply for the role and meet the essential criteria as listed in the attached Job Description for that vacancy. This vacancy is expected to attract a high volume of applications. Therefore, under the Disability Confident Scheme, only disabled people who apply under the scheme and best meet the essential criteria will be offered an interview Documents Library Experience Co-ordinator - JD.pdf (171.10 KB) Candidate Pack.pdf (9.16 MB) Apply Now Apply Now Details Location: Manchester All Saints Campus Faculty / Function: Academic Services Salary: Grade 6 (£31,236 to £34,610) Closing Date: 15 October 2026 Contract Type: Permanent Contracted Hours per week: 35 Benefits 25 days leave + Christmas closure + Bank holidays (Extra 5 days after 5 years of service) Travel loan Wellbeing platform Life insurance Access to Campus Facilities Enhanced parental leave High-quality guaranteed pension Hybrid working opportunities Meet the recruiter Claire Muir ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk Loading Start at the next stage of your career Find out more about our opportunities, or get in touch to discuss bringing your expertise to a university where you'll be supported and valued. Explore our vacancies Get in touch Get in touch Manchester Metropolitan University All Saints Building Manchester M15 6BH United Kingdom ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk +44 (0)161 247 6820 Facebook icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Facebook Twitter icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Twitter YouTube icon Manchester Metropolitan University on YouTube LinkedIn icon Manchester Metropolitan University on LinkedIn Instagram icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Instagram Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply About us Search Get in touch Policies, regulations and legal notices Cookies Website terms of use Accessibility Freedom of information Governance of the University Modern slavery © 2026 Manchester Metropolitan University, all rights reserved."
    },
    "https://manmetjobs.mmu.ac.uk/jobs/vacancy/faculty-pro-vice-chancellor-business-and-law--9471-manchester-all-saints-campus/9370/description/": {
      "title": "Faculty Pro-Vice-Chancellor Business and Law",
      "description": "Faculty Pro-Vice-Chancellor Business and Law  - (9471) | Manchester Metropolitan University Careers CareerZone - Faculty Pro-Vice-Chancellor Business and Law  (9471) Open toolbar Accessibility Grayscale High contrast Negative contrast Light background Links underline Readable font Reset Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Faculty Pro-Vice-Chancellor Business and Law  - (9471) Manchester Metropolitan University is ambitious, values‑driven and forward‑looking. Recently named Times and Sunday Times Modern University of the Year 2026 and recognised nationally for student satisfaction, outstanding research strengths, sustainability and colleague experience, the University is making significant investments in its people, estate and research capacity as part of its Building on our Success: The Road to 2035 Strategy. The University is now seeking an exceptional academic leader to become its next Faculty Pro‑Vice‑Chancellor for Business and Law. This is a significant appointment at a pivotal moment in Manchester Met's development, offering the opportunity to lead a vibrant, diverse and highly successful Faculty while contributing to institutional leadership as a member of the University Executive Group. The Faculty of Business and Law brings together the internationally recognised Manchester Law School, a triple-accredited Business School ranked among the top 1% globally, and the Centre for Enterprise, which works with businesses, policymakers and partners across the country to drive innovation and support sustainable economic growth. Educating more than 10,000 students each year, the Faculty combines consistently strong student outcomes with research that addresses significant challenges facing business, law and society. Through close partnerships with employers, professional bodies, policymakers and civic organisations, it makes an important contribution to economic growth, innovation and social progress. As Faculty Pro‑Vice‑Chancellor, you will provide visible and inclusive leadership, setting a clear direction and creating an environment in which colleagues and students can thrive. You will work closely with senior leaders across the University to implement strategy, strengthen reputation, performance and impact, and grow the Faculty's national and international profile, including its contribution to the generation, dissemination and translation of knowledge. To achieve this, we are seeking an experienced and inspirational academic leader with a strong international academic profile, a deep understanding of the higher education landscape, and a genuine commitment to people‑led leadership. You will bring strategic vision, operational excellence and energy, with the ability to lead complex academic communities, build meaningful partnerships and deliver excellent education and excellent research with impact. We are committed to equity, diversity and inclusion and warmly encourage applications from candidates from underrepresented groups. Further information *Please do not apply for this vacancy via the university website* Further information, including a detailed candidate pack, along with instructions on how to apply, can be found through our executive recruitment advisors (Odgers), via this link - www.odgers.com/96167 - Closing date: 5pm on Friday 16 October 2026 - Interview date: Tuesday 8 December 2026 in Manchester Manchester Metropolitan University fosters an inclusive culture of belonging that promotes equity and celebrates diversity. We value a diverse workforce for the innovation and diversity of thought it brings and welcome applications from all local and international communities, including Black, Asian, and Minority Ethnic backgrounds, disabled people, and LGBTQ+ individuals. We support a range of flexible working arrangements, including hybrid and tailored schedules, which can be discussed with your line manager. If you require reasonable adjustments during the recruitment process or in your role, please let us know so we can provide appropriate support. Our commitment to inclusivity includes mentoring programmes, accessibility resources, and professional development opportunities to empower and support underrepresented groups. Manchester Met is a Disability Confident Leader and, under this scheme, aims to offer an interview to disabled people who apply for the role and meet the essential criteria as listed in the attached Job Description for that vacancy . #LI-CF1 Apply Now Apply Now Details Location: Manchester All Saints Campus Faculty / Function: Business & Law Closing Date: 16 October 2026 Contract Type: Permanent Contracted Hours per week: 37 Benefits 35 days leave + Christmas closure + Bank holidays Travel loan Private medical care (BUPA) Wellbeing platform Life insurance Access to Campus Facilities Enhanced parental leave High-quality guaranteed pension Meet the recruiter Carlos Favario ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk Loading Start at the next stage of your career Find out more about our opportunities, or get in touch to discuss bringing your expertise to a university where you'll be supported and valued. Explore our vacancies Get in touch Get in touch Manchester Metropolitan University All Saints Building Manchester M15 6BH United Kingdom ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk +44 (0)161 247 6820 Facebook icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Facebook Twitter icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Twitter YouTube icon Manchester Metropolitan University on YouTube LinkedIn icon Manchester Metropolitan University on LinkedIn Instagram icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Instagram Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply About us Search Get in touch Policies, regulations and legal notices Cookies Website terms of use Accessibility Freedom of information Governance of the University Modern slavery © 2026 Manchester Metropolitan University, all rights reserved. Cookie Preferences This site uses cookies and other tracking technologies to improve your browsing experience, show personalised content/ads and analyse site traffic. Select cookies to accept Required cookies These cookies are used to ensure the user has a secure journey through the site. earcusessionid - Used to maintain your session. earcusession - Used to secure your session. earcucc - Used to manage your cookie preferences. Analytics Cookies Analytics cookies or performance cookies are used to track website visitors and their user behaviour. _ga - Used by Google Analytics. _gid - Used by Google Analytics. _gat - Used by Google Analytics. _fbp - Used by Meta (Facebook) Pixel. Accept Cookies Accept All Cookies Customise Cookies Reject All Optional"
    },
    "https://manmetjobs.mmu.ac.uk/jobs/vacancy/faculty-pro-vice-chancellor-health-and-education--9472-manchester-birley-campus/9371/description/": {
      "title": "Faculty Pro-Vice-Chancellor Health and Education",
      "description": "Faculty Pro-Vice-Chancellor Health and Education  - (9472) | Manchester Metropolitan University Careers CareerZone - Faculty Pro-Vice-Chancellor Health and Education  (9472) Open toolbar Accessibility Grayscale High contrast Negative contrast Light background Links underline Readable font Reset Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Faculty Pro-Vice-Chancellor Health and Education  - (9472) Manchester Metropolitan University is ambitious, values‑driven and forward‑looking. Recently named Times and Sunday Times Modern University of the Year 2026 and recognised nationally for student satisfaction, outstanding research strengths, sustainability and colleague experience, the University is making significant investments in its people, estate and research capacity as part of its Building on our Success: The Road to 2035 Strategy. The University is now seeking an exceptional academic leader to become its next Faculty Pro‑Vice‑Chancellor for Health and Education. This is a significant appointment at a pivotal moment in Manchester Met's development, offering the opportunity to lead one of the UK's leading health and education faculties while contributing to institutional leadership as a member of the University Executive Group. The Faculty of Health and Education is a dynamic and distinctive academic community spanning Education, Nursing and Public Health, Psychology, Health Professions, and Social Care and Social Work. Educating the next generation of teachers, nurses, allied health professionals, psychologists, sport scientists and other professionals, the Faculty plays a vital role in improving lives and strengthening communities. Through close partnerships with the NHS, schools, local authorities, professional bodies and industry, it is helping address some of society's most pressing challenges. The Faculty is in an exceptionally strong position, with consistently high National Student Survey results and a research profile that delivers real-world impact across health, education, sport and psychology. Education was ranked among the top 10 nationally for research power in REF 2021, reflecting the quality, scale and influence of its research, while a strong culture of interdisciplinary collaboration and external partnership underpins its continued success. As Faculty Pro‑Vice‑Chancellor, you will provide visible and inclusive leadership, setting a clear direction and creating an environment in which colleagues and students can thrive. You will lead a vibrant academic community across an inspiring estate that combines state‑of‑the‑art facilities with buildings rich in heritage and character, while working closely with senior leaders across the University to implement strategy, strengthen reputation, performance and impact, and grow the Faculty's national and international profile. To achieve this, we are seeking an experienced and inspirational academic leader with a strong international academic profile, a deep understanding of the higher education landscape, and a genuine commitment to people‑led leadership. You will bring strategic vision, operational excellence and energy, with the ability to lead complex academic communities, build meaningful partnerships and deliver excellent education and excellent research with impact. We are committed to equity, diversity and inclusion and warmly encourage applications from candidates from underrepresented groups. Further information *Please do not apply for this vacancy via the university website* Further information, including a detailed candidate pack, along with instructions on how to apply, can be found through our executive recruitment advisors (Odgers), via this link - www.odgers.com/96168 - Closing date: 5pm on Friday 16 October 2026 . - Interview date: Thursday 17 December 2026 in Manchester Manchester Metropolitan University fosters an inclusive culture of belonging that promotes equity and celebrates diversity. We value a diverse workforce for the innovation and diversity of thought it brings and welcome applications from all local and international communities, including Black, Asian, and Minority Ethnic backgrounds, disabled people, and LGBTQ+ individuals. We support a range of flexible working arrangements, including hybrid and tailored schedules, which can be discussed with your line manager. If you require reasonable adjustments during the recruitment process or in your role, please let us know so we can provide appropriate support. Our commitment to inclusivity includes mentoring programmes, accessibility resources, and professional development opportunities to empower and support underrepresented groups. Manchester Met is a Disability Confident Leader and, under this scheme, aims to offer an interview to disabled people who apply for the role and meet the essential criteria as listed in the attached Job Description for that vacancy . #LI-CF1 Apply Now Apply Now Details Location: Manchester Birley Campus Faculty / Function: Health & Education Closing Date: 16 October 2026 Contract Type: Permanent Contracted Hours per week: 37 Benefits 35 days leave + Christmas closure + Bank holidays Travel loan Private medical care (BUPA) Wellbeing platform Life insurance Access to Campus Facilities Enhanced parental leave High-quality guaranteed pension Meet the recruiter Carlos Favario ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk Loading Start at the next stage of your career Find out more about our opportunities, or get in touch to discuss bringing your expertise to a university where you'll be supported and valued. Explore our vacancies Get in touch Get in touch Manchester Metropolitan University All Saints Building Manchester M15 6BH United Kingdom ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk +44 (0)161 247 6820 Facebook icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Facebook Twitter icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Twitter YouTube icon Manchester Metropolitan University on YouTube LinkedIn icon Manchester Metropolitan University on LinkedIn Instagram icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Instagram Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply About us Search Get in touch Policies, regulations and legal notices Cookies Website terms of use Accessibility Freedom of information Governance of the University Modern slavery © 2026 Manchester Metropolitan University, all rights reserved. Cookie Preferences This site uses cookies and other tracking technologies to improve your browsing experience, show personalised content/ads and analyse site traffic. Select cookies to accept Required cookies These cookies are used to ensure the user has a secure journey through the site. earcusessionid - Used to maintain your session. earcusession - Used to secure your session. earcucc - Used to manage your cookie preferences. Analytics Cookies Analytics cookies or performance cookies are used to track website visitors and their user behaviour. _ga - Used by Google Analytics. _gid - Used by Google Analytics. _gat - Used by Google Analytics. _fbp - Used by Meta (Facebook) Pixel. Accept Cookies Accept All Cookies Customise Cookies Reject All Optional"
    },
    "https://manmetjobs.mmu.ac.uk/jobs/vacancy/academic-and-study-skills-tutor-9564-manchester-all-saints-campus/9460/description/": {
      "title": "Academic and Study Skills Tutor",
      "description": "Academic and Study Skills Tutor - (9564) | Manchester Metropolitan University Careers CareerZone - Academic and Study Skills Tutor (9564) Open toolbar Accessibility Grayscale High contrast Negative contrast Light background Links underline Readable font Reset Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Academic and Study Skills Tutor - (9564) We're seeking a dynamic and forward-thinking Academic and Study Skills Tutor to join our creative and collaborative team of learning development specialists. This is a full-time, permanent role offering the successful candidate the opportunity to shape impactful learning experiences. We're looking for someone who thrives on innovation, takes initiative, and is passionate about empowering students through a student-centred approach to learning. Our tutors are innovative educators who actively shape the development and delivery of Learning Development provision. They design and lead diverse teaching and learning activities that promote academic success and enrich the student experience. Ultimately, through creative approaches and collaborative practice, they empower students to take ownership of their learning and excel at Manchester Metropolitan University. We're especially keen to hear from candidates who bring fresh perspectives, diverse professional backgrounds, and a proactive, solutions-focused mindset. If you're passionate about inclusive education and empowering students to thrive, and you hold a degree and a relevant teaching qualification (e.g. PGCert or FHEA), we'd love to receive your application. What does the role involve? As an Academic and Study Skills Tutor, you'll work with students across all levels and disciplines in a variety of settings from one-to-one tutorials to group sessions. We teach both on-campus and online to support students' academic development by: designing and embedding study skills and academic literacy sessions within credit-bearing degree courses. leading and enhancing our co-curricular offer, including workshops, short courses, one-to-one tutorials, and online resources. creating engaging digital and multimodal materials that encourage independent learning and enhance our team's offer. developing and leading projects that enrich the student experience and drive continuous improvement. adopting research-informed, reflective practice to shape teaching and contribute to service development. championing inclusive, student-centred education and collaborating creatively with stakeholders including students, academics, and other professional service colleagues. responding proactively to changing demands, prioritising effectively to meet deadlines and deliver high-impact outcomes. What is the working pattern? Our working pattern is designed to support the student experience and service demands. We currently operate with one remote day during term time and three remote days outside of term time. Days are allocated through a team-wide rota that is consistent throughout the year. Core service hours are 8:45am to 5pm. Some flexibility in terms of days and working hours may be required to meet service demands. How do I apply? To submit your application, please click the “Apply Now” button. Applications will only be accepted through our online recruitment portal. Please upload the following documents: a CV (maximum three pages). a cover letter (maximum two pages), clearly demonstrating how you meet the criteria set out in the person specification. To ensure fairness and consistency, the shortlisting panel will not review any content beyond the specified page limits outlined above. Due to the expected high volume of applications, we may need to close this advert earlier than the stated deadline. We therefore encourage you to apply as soon as possible. What are the next steps? Long-listed candidates will be invited to complete a recorded video interview based on elements of the job description. Candidates who are successful at the video interview stage will then be invited to attend an in person interview. We anticipate holding these interviews on Wednesday 25 November 2026. While this date is currently indicative, candidates should be aware that opportunities to reschedule may be limited. Any questions? For informal enquiries, please contact Dr Chad McDonald (Senior Academic and Study Skills Tutor) at c.mcdonald@mmu.ac.uk and Dr Avril Buchanan (Head of Academic and Study Skills) at a.buchanan@mmu.ac.uk Further information Manchester Metropolitan University fosters an inclusive culture of belonging that promotes equity and celebrates diversity. We value a diverse workforce for the innovation and diversity of thought it brings and welcome applications from all local and international communities, including Black, Asian, and Minority Ethnic backgrounds, disabled people, and LGBTQ+ individuals. We support a range of flexible working arrangements, including hybrid and tailored schedules, which can be discussed with your line manager. If you require reasonable adjustments during the recruitment process or in your role, please let us know so we can provide appropriate support. Our commitment to inclusivity includes mentoring programmes, accessibility resources, and professional development opportunities to empower and support underrepresented groups. Manchester Met is a Disability Confident Leader and, under this scheme, aims to offer an interview to disabled people who apply for the role and meet the essential criteria as listed in the attached Job Description for that vacancy. This vacancy is expected to attract a high volume of applications. Therefore, under the Disability Confident Scheme, only disabled people who apply under the scheme and best meet the essential criteria will be offered an interview. Documents Job Description - 002000.1 Academic and Study Skills Tutor.pdf (136.00 KB) Candidate Pack.pdf (9.16 MB) Apply Now Apply Now Details Location: Manchester All Saints Campus Faculty / Function: Academic Services Salary: Grade 8 (£41,064 to £47,389) Closing Date: 18 October 2026 Contract Type: Permanent Contracted Hours per week: 37 Benefits 35 days leave + Christmas closure + Bank holidays Travel loan Wellbeing platform Life insurance Access to Campus Facilities Enhanced parental leave High-quality guaranteed pension Hybrid working opportunities Meet the recruiter Claire Muir ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk Loading Start at the next stage of your career Find out more about our opportunities, or get in touch to discuss bringing your expertise to a university where you'll be supported and valued. Explore our vacancies Get in touch Get in touch Manchester Metropolitan University All Saints Building Manchester M15 6BH United Kingdom ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk +44 (0)161 247 6820 Facebook icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Facebook Twitter icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Twitter YouTube icon Manchester Metropolitan University on YouTube LinkedIn icon Manchester Metropolitan University on LinkedIn Instagram icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Instagram Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply About us Search Get in touch Policies, regulations and legal notices Cookies Website terms of use Accessibility Freedom of information Governance of the University Modern slavery © 2026 Manchester Metropolitan University, all rights reserved. Cookie Preferences This site uses cookies and other tracking technologies to improve your browsing experience, show personalised content/ads and analyse site traffic. Select cookies to accept Required cookies These cookies are used to ensure the user has a secure journey through the site. earcusessionid - Used to maintain your session. earcusession - Used to secure your session. earcucc - Used to manage your cookie preferences. Analytics Cookies Analytics cookies or performance cookies are used to track website visitors and their user behaviour. _ga - Used by Google Analytics. _gid - Used by Google Analytics. _gat - Used by Google Analytics. _fbp - Used by Meta (Facebook) Pixel. Accept Cookies Accept All Cookies Customise Cookies Reject All Optional"
