    "https://manmetjobs.mmu.ac.uk/jobs/vacancy/executive-pa-9584-manchester-all-saints-campus/9480/description/": {
      "title": "Executive PA",
      "description": "Executive PA - (9584) | Manchester Metropolitan University Careers CareerZone - Executive PA (9584) Open toolbar Accessibility Grayscale High contrast Negative contrast Light background Links underline Readable font Reset Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Executive PA - (9584) Executive Personal Assistant (PA) An exciting opportunity has arisen at Manchester Metropolitan University for an enthusiastic and pro-active Executive Personal Assistant (PA) to support a member(s) of the Senior Executive Team within the University.  This is a position where the right individual can make a difference in a vibrant, busy and fulfilling environment, joining a team of PAs working collaboratively to provide a high level of service to our senior leaders. About the role: The Executive Personal Assistant is a pivotal role, providing confidential, efficient and effective high-level administration support to the academic Senior Executive in the University's Leadership Team. You will work within a great team of Executive PAs and take a proactive approach to ensure that all tasks are completed to the highest standard whilst assisting with the co-ordination and management of higher-level administrative tasks in line with the University's strategic plans. About you: This is a challenging, fast-paced and varied role that requires a pro-active individual.  You will have excellent organisational skills with meticulous attention to detail and a high level of literacy and numeracy.  Applicants should also be able to exercise discretion, develop solutions to complex problems, and excel in working collaboratively with colleagues across the University. To learn more about role, and benefits, please read the Job Description and Candidate Pack provided below. What we offer: A generous holiday package which includes 25 days per year holiday (increases with service) and bank holidays plus Christmas shutdown Hybrid working – 3 days on campus, 2 days working from home (subject to business need) Salary progression A range of additional reward opportunities A fantastic range of benefits, offers and perks, including discounted gym membership, travel benefits such as our cycle to work scheme, local and national discounts and our employee assistance programme How to Apply: To apply, please submit your CV and a covering letter via our online application portal outlining how your skills and experience evidence: Managing complex diaries and competing priorities Prioritising a varied and complex workload Building stakeholder relationships Please note that only applications including a covering letter may be considered at the shortlisting stage Further information: Manchester Metropolitan University fosters an inclusive culture of belonging that promotes equity and celebrates diversity. We value a diverse workforce for the innovation and diversity of thought it brings and welcome applications from all local and international communities, including Black, Asian, and Minority Ethnic backgrounds, disabled people, and LGBTQ+ individuals. We support a range of flexible working arrangements, including hybrid and tailored schedules, which can be discussed with your line manager. If you require reasonable adjustments during the recruitment process or in your role, please let us know so we can provide appropriate support. Our commitment to inclusivity includes mentoring programmes, accessibility resources, and professional development opportunities to empower and support underrepresented groups. Manchester Met is a Disability Confident Leader and, under this scheme, aims to offer an interview to disabled people who apply for the role and meet the essential criteria as listed in the attached Job Description for that vacancy. This vacancy is expected to attract a high volume of applications. Therefore, under the Disability Confident Scheme, only disabled people who apply under the scheme and best meet the essential criteria will be offered an interview. #LI-MP1 Documents G6  Executive Personal Assistant (1) (002).pdf (291.19 KB) Candidate Pack.pdf (9.15 MB) Apply Now Apply Now Details Location: Manchester All Saints Campus Faculty / Function: Executive Support Team Salary: Grade 6 (£31,236 to £34,610) Closing Date: 18 October 2026 Contract Type: Permanent Contracted Hours per week: 35 Benefits 25 days leave + Christmas closure + Bank holidays (Extra 5 days after 5 years of service) Travel loan Wellbeing platform Life insurance Access to Campus Facilities Enhanced parental leave High-quality guaranteed pension Hybrid working opportunities Meet the recruiter Neha Phanse ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk Loading Start at the next stage of your career Find out more about our opportunities, or get in touch to discuss bringing your expertise to a university where you'll be supported and valued. Explore our vacancies Get in touch Get in touch Manchester Metropolitan University All Saints Building Manchester M15 6BH United Kingdom ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk +44 (0)161 247 6820 Facebook icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Facebook Twitter icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Twitter YouTube icon Manchester Metropolitan University on YouTube LinkedIn icon Manchester Metropolitan University on LinkedIn Instagram icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Instagram Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply About us Search Get in touch Policies, regulations and legal notices Cookies Website terms of use Accessibility Freedom of information Governance of the University Modern slavery © 2026 Manchester Metropolitan University, all rights reserved. Cookie Preferences This site uses cookies and other tracking technologies to improve your browsing experience, show personalised content/ads and analyse site traffic. Select cookie