    "https://manmetjobs.mmu.ac.uk/jobs/vacancy/marketing-officer-future-students-9571-manchester-all-saints-campus/9467/description/": {
      "title": "Marketing Officer (Future Students)",
      "description": "Marketing Officer (Future Students) - (9571) | Manchester Metropolitan University Careers CareerZone - Marketing Officer (Future Students) (9571) Open toolbar Accessibility Grayscale High contrast Negative contrast Light background Links underline Readable font Reset Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Marketing Officer (Future Students) - (9571) At Manchester Met, we are ambitious, inclusive and focused on impact. We work collaboratively as one University to tell clear, engaging stories, build a strong reputation and support students to transform their lives. Together, we are shaping futures locally and globally. It is an exciting time to join us. We have been named Modern University of the Year for the second consecutive year, recognised as an Outstanding Workplace , and ranked the number one sustainable university for a record‑breaking fourth year. Our commitment to people, progress and purpose shapes how we work and what we deliver. We are now recruiting for three Marketing Officer positions in the Future Students Marketing team: x2 Marketing Officer (Permanent) – supporting undergraduate and postgraduate student recruitment for the Faculty of Health and Education . x1 Marketing Officer (12-month fixed-term contract) – supporting postgraduate student recruitment for the Faculty of Science and Engineering . You will work closely with colleagues across External Relations and the Faculty supporting undergraduate and postgraduate recruitment through targeted, insight‑led marketing activity in a competitive environment. The roles offer the opportunity to develop subject‑aligned marketing expertise, collaborate with academic and professional services colleagues, and contribute across the full recruitment journey. Your work will support University priorities by helping prospective students understand their options and see themselves at Manchester Met. The teams follow a hybrid working pattern, with an expectation of two days per week on campus (typically Tuesday and Wednesday) and the remainder working from home, with occasional additional campus attendance required for meetings and out of hours working for events. What you'll do Working with the Marketing Manager for either the Faculty of Science and Engineering or Faculty of Health and Education, you will plan and deliver recruitment marketing that supports the Future Students strategy and faculty objectives. You will: Plan and deliver strategic and tactical marketing activity for either undergraduate or postgraduate recruitment in the Faculty. Manage a varied subject portfolio and create content that supports applicants at different stages of the recruitment journey. Lead marketing campaigns and projects, coordinating activity across teams and channels. Deliver and manage digital marketing activity, including PPC and display advertising. Produce high‑quality, audience‑focused content for digital and offline channels, ensuring brand, accessibility and quality standards are met. Manage and update sections of the University website using the CMS to improve usability and performance. Support recruitment events and conversion activity in collaboration with faculty and Future Students colleagues. Use insight, data and reporting to evaluate activity and inform future planning. Act as a brand champion, ensuring consistent, accurate and compliant use of the Manchester Met brand. Who we're looking for We are looking for a proactive marketing professional who enjoys working in a complex, fast‑paced environment and building effective working relationships. You will bring: Professional marketing experience, ideally within a large or complex organisation. Experience delivering integrated marketing campaigns across digital and offline channels. Strong copywriting, content creation and editorial skills. Experience using paid and organic digital marketing tactics. Confidence working with data, insight and reporting to demonstrate impact and inform decisions. Strong organisational and project management skills, with the ability to manage competing priorities. A collaborative approach and experience working with academic and professional services colleagues. You will be curious, solutions‑focused and committed to delivering high‑quality marketing that supports prospective students to make informed choices. Application & Assessment To apply, submit your CV and cover letter (not longer than 2 pages) outlining how best you met the criteria, via our online portal. Please note applications received without a cover letter will not be considered. Assessment will include a competency-based task and an interview, and the assessments are expected to take place during the week commencing 9 November. Due to the volume of applications, we receive, we sometimes close our vacancies early. It is therefore advisable to apply as early as possible if you would like to be considered for a role. We welcome questions about the role, however, all expressions of interest should be included as part of your application (e.g. within your cover letter) and submitted through the application portal, not via email. For any further essential enquiries about these vacancies, please contact Lucy Moss - l.moss@mmu.ac.uk (Marketing Manager, Health and Education) and  Rebecca Bradshaw (Marketing Manager, Science and Engineering) – r.bradshaw@mmu.ac.uk . Further Information Manchester Metropolitan University fosters an inclusive culture of belonging that promotes equity and celebrates diversity. We value a diverse workforce for the innovation and diversity of thought it brings and welcome applications from local and international communities, including those from Black, Asian, and Minority Ethnic backgrounds, disabled people, and LGBTQ+ individuals. We support a range of flexible working arrangements, including hybrid and tailored schedules, which can be discussed with your line manager. If you require reasonable adjustments during the recruitment process or in your role, please let us know so we can provide appropriate support. Our commitment to inclusivity includes mentoring programmes, accessibility resources, and professional development opportunities to empower and support underrepresented groups. Manchester Met is a Disability Confident Leader and, under this scheme, aims to offer an interview to disabled people who apply for the role and meet the essential criteria as listed in the attached Job Description for that vacancy. This vacancy is expected to attract a high volume of applications. Therefore, under the Disability Confident Scheme, only disabled people who apply under the scheme and best meet the essential criteria will be offered an interview. Documents Marketing Officer (Future Students) JD for Faculty of H&E.pdf (125.54 KB) Marketing Officer (Future Students) JD for Faculty of S&E.pdf (125.72 KB) Candidate Pack.pdf (9.15 MB) Apply Now Apply Now Details Location: Manchester All Saints Campus Faculty / Function: External Relations Salary: Grade 7 (£35,608 to £39,906) Closing Date: 18 October 2026 Contract Type: Permanent Contracted Hours per week: 35 Benefits 25 days leave + Christmas closure + Bank holidays (Extra 5 days after 5 years of service) Travel loan Wellbeing platform Life insurance Access to Campus Facilities Enhanced parental leave High-quality guaranteed pension Hybrid working opportunities Meet the recruiter Neha Phanse ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk Loading Start at the next stage of your career Find out more about our opportunities, or get in touch to discuss bringing your expertise to a university where you'll be supported and valued. Explore our vacancies Get in touch Get in touch Manchester Metropolitan University All Saints Building Manchester M15 6BH United Kingdom ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk +44 (0)161 247 6820 Facebook icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Facebook Twitter icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Twitter YouTube icon Manchester Metropolitan University on YouTube LinkedIn icon Manchester Metropolitan University on LinkedIn Instagram icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Instagram Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply About us Search Get in touch Policies, regulations and legal notices Cookies Website terms of use Accessibility Freedom of information Governance of the University Modern slavery © 2026 Manchester Metropolitan University, all rights reserved. Cookie Preferences This site uses cookies and other tracking technologies to improve your browsing experience, show personalised content/ads and analyse site traffic. Select cookies to accept Required cookies These cookies are used to ensure the user has a secure journey through the site. earcusessionid - Used to maintain your session. earcusession - Used to secure your session. earcucc - Used to manage your cookie preferences. Analytics Cookies Analytics cookies or performance cookies are used to track website visitors and their user behaviour. _ga - Used by Google Analytics. _gid - Used by Google Analytics. _gat - Used by Google Analytics. _fbp - Used by Meta (Facebook) Pixel. Accept Cookies Accept All Cookies Customise Cookies Reject All Optional"
