    "https://manmetjobs.mmu.ac.uk/jobs/vacancy/research-associate-impact-9568-manchester-all-saints-campus/9464/description/": {
      "title": "Research Associate (Impact) -",
      "description": "Research Associate (Impact) - (9568) | Manchester Metropolitan University Careers CareerZone - Research Associate (Impact) (9568) Open toolbar Accessibility Grayscale High contrast Negative contrast Light background Links underline Readable font Reset Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Research Associate (Impact) - (9568) The Department of People and Performance at Manchester Metropolitan University is based in its Business School and, drawing on innovative research and teaching techniques, offers specialist accredited undergraduate and postgraduate programmes in human resource management, business psychology and sport business and marketing management. It houses the Centre for Decent Work and Productivity | Manchester Met (mmu.ac.uk) where researchers investigate what causes of - and who has - decent and productive work and what can be done to shape a bright future for the world of work. The centre is nationally and internationally recognised for its work in this area, with many leading scholars who hold prestigious research grants, publish in high-quality journals and create substantial impact on policy and practice. The role The Department is seeking to appoint a Research Associate (Grade 7) to support with developing and tracking impact for two of its research projects which, it is anticipated, will be impact case studies for REF2029. Details of these can be found at the links below: Research: Creating an adult social care workforce strategy for Cornwall | Manchester Metropolitan University Research: Gender pay gaps in medicine | Manchester Metropolitan University The Research Associate will support the research team in: Producing an adult social care workforce strategy implementation framework/toolkit, drawing on existing research that underpins a local authority strategy co-written by centre members. Rolling out of the toolkit to other local authorities. Tracking dissemination and citations, and compiling a comprehensive evidence file related to the Gender Pay Gap project, with associated metrics, and producing an impact report. About you You will have experience of translating research into impact by writing toolkits and/or producing reports for policy and practitioner audiences. You will also have experience of working with these outputs with external stakeholders to generate impact. You will possess a well-developed knowledge of the health and social care system in England. You will be able to demonstrate a track record of effective project management and communication with a range of stakeholders and collaborators. Essential skills Hold or be working towards a relevant doctoral level qualification Ability to synthesise complex data from different sources and communicate findings orally and via written reports and articles for a range of diverse audiences. Ability to use initiative and judgement to develop appropriate techniques in order to facilitate research work and resolve problems affecting the achievement of objectives and deadlines. Possessing sufficient breadth or depth of knowledge of health and social care in England to work within the research and impact programme. Further information For an informal discussion about this role, please contact Professor Carol Atkinson via c.d.atkinson@mmu.ac.uk Interviews will take place on 12 November Manchester Metropolitan University fosters an inclusive culture of belonging that promotes equity and celebrates diversity. We value a diverse workforce for the innovation and diversity of thought it brings and welcome applications from all local and international communities, including Black, Asian, and Minority Ethnic backgrounds, disabled people, and LGBTQ+ individuals. We support a range of flexible working arrangements, including hybrid and tailored schedules, which can be discussed with your line manager. If you require reasonable adjustments during the recruitment process or in your role, please let us know so we can provide appropriate support. Our commitment to inclusivity includes mentoring programmes, accessibility resources, and professional development opportunities to empower and support underrepresented groups. Manchester Met is a Disability Confident Leader and, under this scheme, aims to offer an interview to disabled people who apply for the role and meet the essential criteria as listed in the attached Job Description for that vacancy. Documents Job Description.pdf (70.54 KB) Candidate Pack.pdf (9.15 MB) Apply Now Apply Now Details Location: Manchester All Saints Campus Faculty / Function: Business & Law Salary: Grade 7 (£36,320 to £40,704) Pro Rata Closing Date: 27 October 2026 Contract Type: Fixed Term Contract Length: 6 months Contracted Hours per week: 17.5 Benefits 35 days leave + Christmas closure + Bank holidays Travel loan Wellbeing platform Life insurance Access to Campus Facilities Enhanced parental leave High-quality guaranteed pension Meet the recruiter Michelle Legg ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk Loading Start at the next stage of your career Find out more about our opportunities, or get in touch to discuss bringing your expertise to a university where you'll be supported and valued. Explore our vacancies Get in touch Get in touch Manchester Metropolitan University All Saints Building Manchester M15 6BH United Kingdom ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk +44 (0)161 247 6820 Facebook icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Facebook Twitter icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Twitter YouTube icon Manchester Metropolitan University on YouTube LinkedIn icon Manchester Metropolitan University on LinkedIn Instagram icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Instagram Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply About us Search Get in touch Policies, regulations and legal notices Cookies Website terms of use Accessibility Freedom of information Governance of the University Modern slavery © 2026 Manchester Metropolitan University, all rights reserved."
    },
    "https://manmetjobs.mmu.ac.uk/jobs/vacancy/senior-lecturer-in-digital-finance-and-fintech-9262-manchester-all-saints-campus/9171/description/": {
      "title": "Senior Lecturer in Digital Finance and Fintech -",
      "description": "Senior Lecturer in Digital Finance and Fintech - (9262) | Manchester Metropolitan University Careers CareerZone - Senior Lecturer in Digital Finance and Fintech (9262) Open toolbar Accessibility Grayscale High contrast Negative contrast Light background Links underline Readable font Reset Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Senior Lecturer in Digital Finance and Fintech - (9262) Shape the future of finance at a Triple-Accredited Business School! Interested in making a change from industry? Do you have a passion for working with students? If so, why not join our Department of Finance and Economics. About You We are seeking enthusiastic and forward-thinking academics to join us as senior lecturers in digital finance and fintech. We want to speak to people with relevant subject expertise, a passion for developing others and creative and collaborative mindsets. You will: Have current industry experience in blockchain development, quantitative financial analysis, regtech or fintech data science Have a desire to shape our future curriculum and extend our existing portfolio of programmes to align with future needs Be passionate about supporting students into great graduate roles. Be committed to maintaining your external profile and contributing to the wider academic and professional community. About Us Our department is one of the largest and most vibrant Finance and Economics departments in the UK, with over 2,000 students and more than 80 academic staff. Our triple accreditation places us in the top 1% of business schools worldwide - a mark of excellence in both education and research. We are currently focused on: Delivering a refreshed portfolio of undergraduate and postgraduate programmes. Expanding into emerging and interdisciplinary areas aligned with our strategic priorities and the future needs of graduate employers Innovating in Learning, Teaching and Assessment to meet the evolving needs of students and employers (including the integration of AI and the development of future-facing skills). Why Join Us? You'll be part of a dynamic, fast-paced department that places student success and graduate outcomes at the heart of everything we do. Collaboration is central to our culture, within the department and across the Business School, providing you with the opportunity to contribute to energetic and expert teams. If you're passionate about shaping the next generation of finance professionals and contributing to a department that values innovation, impact, and excellence, we'd love to hear from you. Please feel free to send any informal enquiries to Anna Egan (Head of Department) via a.egan@mmu.ac.uk Formal applications should be submitted via our recruitment portal. Please submit a CV and Cover Letter only. The cover letter should be no more than 300 words in length. Successful candidates will be invited to do the following: Take part in an interview with members of the department's senior leadership team. Deliver a 15 min presentation (with an additional 10 min Q&A time) to members of the department on a topic of the department's choosing. Find out more about our story and explore our campus ! Manchester Metropolitan University fosters an inclusive culture of belonging that promotes equity and celebrates diversity. We value a diverse workforce for the innovation and diversity of thought it brings and welcome applications from all local and international communities, including Black, Asian, and Minority Ethnic backgrounds, disabled people, and LGBTQ+ individuals. We support a range of flexible working arrangements, including hybrid and tailored schedules, which can be discussed with your line manager. If you require reasonable adjustments during the recruitment process or in your role, please let us know so we can provide appropriate support. Our commitment to inclusivity includes mentoring programmes, accessibility resources, and professional development opportunities to empower and support underrepresented groups. Manchester Met is a Disability Confident Leader and, under this scheme, aims to offer an interview to disabled people who apply for the role and meet the essential criteria as listed in the attached Job Description for that vacancy. #LI-CF1 Documents 9262 Senior Lecturer in Digital Finance and FinTech EPC.pdf (196.48 KB) Apply Now Apply Now Details Location: Manchester All Saints Campus Faculty / Function: Business & Law Salary: Grade 9 Closing Date: 27 October 2026 Contract Type: Permanent Contracted Hours per week: 37 Benefits 35 days leave + Christmas closure + Bank holidays Travel loan Wellbeing platform Life insurance Access to Campus Facilities Enhanced parental leave High-quality guaranteed pension Meet the recruiter Neha Phanse ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk Loading Start at the next stage of your career Find out more about our opportunities, or get in touch to discuss bringing your expertise to a university where you'll be supported and valued. Explore our vacancies Get in touch Get in touch Manchester Metropolitan University All Saints Building Manchester M15 6BH United Kingdom ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk +44 (0)161 247 6820 Facebook icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Facebook Twitter icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Twitter YouTube icon Manchester Metropolitan University on YouTube LinkedIn icon Manchester Metropolitan University on LinkedIn Instagram icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Instagram Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply About us Search Get in touch Policies, regulations and legal notices Cookies Website terms of use Accessibility Freedom of information Governance of the University Modern slavery © 2026 Manchester Metropolitan University, all rights reserved."
    },
    "https://manmetjobs.mmu.ac.uk/jobs/vacancy/tutor-in-accounting-and-finance-9256-manchester-all-saints-campus/9165/description/": {
      "title": "Tutor in Accounting and Finance",
      "description": "Tutor in Accounting and Finance - (9256) | Manchester Metropolitan University Careers CareerZone - Tutor in Accounting and Finance (9256) Open toolbar Accessibility Grayscale High contrast Negative contrast Light background Links underline Readable font Reset Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Tutor in Accounting and Finance - (9256) The Department of Finance and Economics sits within the triple accredited (AACSB, AMBA, EQUIS) Business School in Manchester Metropolitan University. We are a large and ambitious department, with a core focus of delivering excellent education that supports our students into great graduate outcomes. We deliver a diverse portfolio of undergraduate and postgraduate programmes that blend work integrated learning with a research and practice informed syllabus. Currently, we are specifically seeking to recruit a Permanent Academic Tutor to support our Learning, Teaching and Assessment activity in a range of subjects across our Accounting and Finance provision. Currently, we are particularly interested in working with candidates who have an expertise in Financial Reporting and Corporate Finance. We welcome applications from candidates who have sustained experience of delivery and assessment in these subject areas, while also recognising that the breadth of our portfolio will provide opportunities to support additional subjects. We would love to hear from you if you have: Subject expertise in Financial Reporting and Corporate Finance. Prior experience of teaching or training in these subject areas. A passion for innovative and interactive teaching focused on student success. An enthusiasm for working in large teams. An interest in supporting key student success initiatives. Alongside teaching and marking responsibilities, our academic tutors also benefit from opportunities to support department initiatives focused on our student success priorities, including graduate outcomes and student satisfaction. The nature of this role allows the successful candidate to really immerse themselves in the department as a result of the volume of on-campus activity they will contribute too. For informal discussion about the role please contact Anna Egan (Head of Department) at a.egan@mmu.ac.uk Interested applicants should submit a CV and a cover letter (max 1 page) outlining how their experience aligns with the above identified requirements of the role. Why Join Manchester Met? At Manchester Metropolitan University , we are proud to foster an inclusive culture of belonging that promotes equity, celebrates diversity, and values the different perspectives a diverse workforce brings. We warmly encourage applications from all communities, including candidates from Black, Asian and Minority Ethnic backgrounds, disabled people, and LGBTQ+ individuals. We support flexible working arrangements, including hybrid and tailored schedules, and are committed to ensuring colleagues can thrive in their roles. If you require reasonable adjustments during the recruitment process or employment, we will work with you to provide appropriate support. Our commitment to inclusion is reflected through mentoring programmes, accessibility resources, and professional development opportunities designed to empower underrepresented groups. As a Disability Confident Leader , Manchester Met aims to offer an interview to disabled applicants who meet the essential criteria outlined in the Job Description #LI-CF1 Documents 9256 Academic Tutor.pdf (274.24 KB) Apply Now Apply Now Details Location: Manchester All Saints Campus Faculty / Function: Business & Law Salary: Grade 7 Closing Date: 27 October 2026 Contract Type: Permanent Contracted Hours per week: 35 Benefits 25 days leave + Christmas closure + Bank holidays (Extra 5 days after 5 years of service) Travel loan Wellbeing platform Life insurance Access to Campus Facilities Enhanced parental leave High-quality guaranteed pension Meet the recruiter Neha Phanse ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk Loading Start at the next stage of your career Find out more about our opportunities, or get in touch to discuss bringing your expertise to a university where you'll be supported and valued. Explore our vacancies Get in touch Get in touch Manchester Metropolitan University All Saints Building Manchester M15 6BH United Kingdom ManMetJobs@mmu.ac.uk +44 (0)161 247 6820 Facebook icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Facebook Twitter icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Twitter YouTube icon Manchester Metropolitan University on YouTube LinkedIn icon Manchester Metropolitan University on LinkedIn Instagram icon Manchester Metropolitan University on Instagram Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply About us Search Get in touch Policies, regulations and legal notices Cookies Website terms of use Accessibility Freedom of information Governance of the University Modern slavery © 2026 Manchester Metropolitan University, all rights reserved. Cookie Preferences This site uses cookies and other tracking technologies to improve your browsing experience, show personalised content/ads and analyse site traffic. Select cookies to accept Required cookies These cookies are used to ensure the user has a secure journey through the site. earcusessionid - Used to maintain your session. earcusession - Used to secure your session. earcucc - Used to manage your cookie preferences. Analytics Cookies Analytics cookies or performance cookies are used to track website visitors and their user behaviour. _ga - Used by Google Analytics. _gid - Used by Google Analytics. _gat - Used by Google Analytics. _fbp - Used by Meta (Facebook) Pixel. Accept Cookies Accept All Cookies Customise Cookies Reject All Optional"
