    "https://manmetjobs.mmu.ac.uk/jobs/vacancy/tutor-in-economics-9258-manchester-all-saints-campus/9167/description/": {
      "title": "Tutor in Economics",
      "description": "Tutor in Economics - (9258) | Manchester Metropolitan University Careers CareerZone - Tutor in Economics (9258) Open toolbar Accessibility Grayscale High contrast Negative contrast Light background Links underline Readable font Reset Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Explore vacancies Working at Manchester Met Living in Manchester How to apply Professorial opportunities Login Tutor in Economics - (9258) The Department of Finance and Economics sits within the triple accredited (AACSB, AMBA, EQUIS) Business School in Manchester Metropolitan University. We are a large and ambitious department, with a core focus of delivering excellent education that supports our students into great graduate outcomes. We deliver a diverse portfolio of undergraduate and postgraduate programmes that blend work integrated learning with a research and practice informed syllabus. Currently, we are specifically seeking to recruit a Permanent Academic Tutor to support our Learning, Teaching and Assessment activity in a range of areas across our Economics provision. You may have expertise in areas such as data analytics, economic history or global political economy. We welcome candidates able to support in any of these areas, but all interested applicants must have an ability to deliver microecnomics or macroeconomics to an intermediate level. We would love to hear from you if you have: Expertise in either microeconomics or macroeconomics with prior experience of teaching or related practice. A passion for innovative and interactive teaching focused on student success. An enthusiasm for working in large teams. An interest in supporting key student success initiatives. Alongside teaching and marking responsibilities, our academic tutors also benefit from opportunities to support department initiatives focused on our student success priorities, including graduate outcomes and student satisfaction. The nature of this role allows the successful candidate to really immerse themselves in the department as a result of the volume of on-campus activity they will contribute too. For informal discussion about the role please contact Anna Egan (Head of Department) at a.egan@mmu.ac.uk Interested applicants should submit a CV and a cover letter (max 1 page) outlining how their experience aligns with the above identified requirements of the role. Why Join Manchester Met? At Manchester Metropolitan University , we are proud to foster an inclusive culture of belonging that promotes equity, celebrates diversity, and values the different perspectives a diverse workforce brings. We warmly encourage applications from all communities, including candidates from Black, Asian and Minority Ethnic backgrounds, disabled people, and LGBTQ+ individuals. We support flexible working arrangements, including hybrid and tailored schedules, and are committed to ensuring colleagues can thrive in their roles. If you require reasonable adjustments during the recruitment process or employment, we will work with you to provide appropriate support. Our commitment to inclusion is reflected through mentoring programmes, accessibility resources, and professional development opportunities designed to empower underrepresented groups. As a Disability Confident Leader , Manchester Met aims to offer an interview to disabled applicants who meet the essential criteria outlined in the Job Description #LI-CF1 Documents 9258 Academic Tutor.pdf (274.22 KB) Apply Now Apply Now Details Location: Manchester All Saints Campus Faculty / Function: Business & Law Salary: Grade 7 Closing Date: 27 October 2026 Contract Type: Permanent Contracted Hours per week: 35 Benefits 25 days leave + Christmas closure + Bank holidays (Extra 5 days after 5 years of service) Travel loan Wellbeing platform Life insurance Access to Campus Facilities Enhanced parental leave High-quality guaranteed pension Meet the recruiter Neha Phanse Ma